    user_response: "Modify the existing DropAid application without rebuilding it.\n\n1. **Remove the Map from Home:** Completely remove the map currently displayed on the homepage. Keep the homepage clean, professional, and focused on ambulance booking.\n\n2. **Show Map After Booking Initiation:** Display the interactive map only after the user successfully holds the red booking button for 5 seconds or submits a manual booking form. Open the map in the booking/tracking interface immediately after submission.\n\n3. **Accurate Location:** Center the map on the user\'s actual GPS pickup location, with permission, or their manually selected pickup point. Display the pickup marker, destination marker, assigned ambulance, and road-following route when available.\n\n4. **Dynamic Tracking:** Initially show the pickup location and ambulance-search status. Display the assigned ambulance and its route after operator acceptance. Update the route and vehicle position as the trip progresses.\n\n**Quality Control:** Ensure both booking methods open the same map interface, preserve booking details, prevent duplicate requests, and handle GPS permission or routing failures gracefully. Verify the map never appears on the homepage and remains accessible throughout the active trip. Preserve existing styling, responsiveness, and working features."
    items {
