    thinking: "**Reviewing Application Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the behavior of the DropAid application, specifically the response after submitting a booking and the subsequent map display. I\'m also reviewing the prompt\'s requirements meticulously, ensuring that I address each point systematically, particularly the part about modifying without rebuilding.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Flow**\n\nI\'ve determined I need to remove the map from the home screen for a cleaner interface. The map should now only appear after a booking is initiated, either by holding the red button or through the manual form. Furthermore, I need to ensure the map centers on the user\'s pickup location, with all pertinent markers and route information. I also aim to have a dynamic tracking display for each booking method. Finally, I\'m checking to make sure both booking methods render the same map and interface.\n\n\n**Analyzing Initial Conditions**\n\nI\'m now diving into the application\'s initial state and confirming the map\'s behavior when a user first launches the application, focusing on the `App.tsx` and how `bookings` is initialized. I\'m reviewing how the demo booking affects the initial map visibility and am checking the logic for `activeBooking`. I\'ll analyze how the map component\'s conditional rendering works to ensure it aligns with the updated requirements.\n\n\n**Clarifying Initial Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the initial state of the application when a user first lands on the homepage. I\'m reviewing `App.tsx` and considering the impact of the `[INITIAL_DEMO_BOOKING]` initialization, realizing it immediately displays an active booking card and map. I\'m checking if the `activeBooking` state determines an \"active trip.\" This is critical to ensure that I address requirements 1 and 2, specifically removing the map from the homepage and displaying it only after a booking is initiated.\n\n\n**Confirming Map Behavior**\n\nI\'m now implementing the map view\'s launch after submitting the booking form to make sure it opens immediately in the booking or tracking interface. I\'m focusing on ensuring the map centers accurately on the user\'s pickup point, displaying markers for pickup, destination, assigned ambulance, and route. Additionally, I\'m working to make sure the app offers dynamic tracking, reflecting pickup and ambulance search statuses, including vehicle routes and positions as the trip progresses. I need to make sure the quality controls are in place.\n\n\n**Verifying Home State**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the initial application state, particularly when a user first launches DropAid. I\'ve re-confirmed that `handleResetSimulation` correctly clears the `bookings` state, ensuring a clean slate. I\'m reviewing how `localStorage` is used to load and persist bookings, and how this impacts the initial view. My aim is to make sure the homepage starts clean with the hold button and manual options if there\'s no active booking.\n\n\n"
