  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Ensuring Clear Map Rendering**\n\nI\'ve been working on ensuring the map renders crisply after a booking submission. I\'m now certain that calling `map.invalidateSize()` after the map mounts will do the trick. Now, I\'m checking when the `pickupCoords` change or on mount, to decide when to trigger this. I\'m currently working to determine the correct conditions.\n\n\n**Confirming User Map Centering**\n\nI\'ve added code to center the map on the user\'s pickup coordinates whenever they change or when the map is ready. I\'m using `setView` to ensure the map is always focused on the relevant location. My code will now guarantee that the map is showing the correct location upon mount and whenever the coordinates are changed!\n\n\n**Defining Booking Initialization**\n\nI\'m now focusing on initializing a booking with all its details. I\'ve broken down the steps involved in `handleCreateBooking`. The booking will start in the `\'pending\'` stage with a unique ID, tracking code, patient info, and location details. The initial state will also include some critical parameters such as equipment requested. Importantly, the `assignedUnitId` is undefined until the operator accepts!\n\n\n**Detailing Booking Initial Attributes**\n\nI\'m now setting up the other crucial booking attributes. The route polyline will initially be empty, so the map shows only pickup and hospital locations. I\'m also adding initial values for ETA (5 minutes), estimated distance (4.8 km), price (calculated), and an empty documents array. I\'m starting a `stageTimestamps` object with a \'requested\' timestamp, too. After setting up these details, I\'ll save this new booking to the bookings state and POST it to the backend. The UI will then update to the booking/tracking view with a toast message. The map will display pickup and hospital markers, along with search status. Finally, I\'m thinking about operator acceptance, and how that will work within the dashboard.\n\n\n**Defining Booking Acceptance Logic**\n\nI\'m now detailing `handleAcceptBooking(bookingId)` and the associated steps. It starts by finding the nearest available ambulance, or defaulting to any available one if the first search fails. This includes determining the actual road route from the ambulance\'s current location to the pickup point. Subsequently, I\'m setting the booking to `\'en_route_pickup\'` and assigning the ambulance, updating the polyline, distance, ETA, and current vehicle position. I\'m also adding an \'accepted\' timestamp.\n\n\n"
