  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Dashboard Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the UserDashboard.tsx file, specifically lines 180-295. My goal is to understand the rendering logic for active bookings. It seems like the condition `activeBooking && activeBooking.stage !== \'completed\' && activeBooking.stage !== \'cancelled\'` is the key. When this evaluates to true, I believe it\'s responsible for triggering the display of the Active Booking & Tracking Screen. I\'m focusing on what happens inside this conditional block next.\n\n\n**Confirming Map Integration**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `<LeafletMap />` can indeed be directly embedded within the tracking card, which seems to be at the heart of the \"Active Booking Live Tracking Interface.\" Looking closer, the code block utilizes a `space-y-4` layout for the top status bar, ambulance search banner (conditionally), and, most importantly, the interactive map viewport. The map itself is set to a fixed height of 460px with rounded corners and a shadow effect.\n\n\n**Observing User Interface Rendering**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the conditional rendering within the active booking section. When `activeBooking` exists, the dedicated tracking interface with the Leaflet map is displayed. Conversely, when `activeBooking` is null, the clean homepage with the 5s Hold button, GPS pickup status, Manual Booking configuration, and Hospital Directory preview is displayed, which renders without the map. Cancelling or completing the trip sets `activeBooking` to null, triggering an immediate return to the homepage.\n\n\n**Mapping Booking Transitions**\n\nI\'m now mapping out how booking transitions trigger UI changes, focusing on what happens when `activeBooking` becomes completed or null, which immediately returns to the clean Homepage, and how this affects saved trip history. I am also investigating the demo reset flow. I am now exploring both booking methods. The 5-second Hold button and Manual Booking form methods both call `onSubmitBooking` with different parameters, but both trigger the Tracking View with the Map. Both methods use the exact same map interface and preserve booking details. I will now examine the `UserDashboard`\'s required props.\n\n\n**Verifying Required Props**\n\nNow, I\'m verifying the props required by `UserDashboard` when `activeBooking` is present, focusing on map-related dependencies. Specifically, I\'m examining the impact of passing props like `ambulances`, `routePolyline`, `routeError`, `onRecalculateRoute`, `onAcceptBooking`, and `onAdvanceStage` into the `<LeafletMap />` component. These will play a role in how the tracking map renders and responds to live updates.\n\n\n**Implementing Pending Stage Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the pending stage. When `activeBooking.stage` is \'pending\', I\'ll show the \"Scanning Fleet\" status and \"Accept Request\" button. I\'m exploring an auto-accept countdown, with either user or system-initiated acceptance using `onAcceptBooking(activeBooking.id)`. This will be in `UserDashboard` or `App`. Once accepted, the stage moves to \'en_route_pickup\' with ambulance assignment, route display, and real-time updates. I\'ll need to check the `OperatorDashboard.tsx` now to evaluate if the map needs to be visible there as well.\n\n\n**Verifying UI Visibility**\n\nI\'m now verifying map visibility across UI states. When `currentView` is \'operator\', a map renders in `App.tsx`. However, on the User Homepage (`currentView === \'user\'` without an active booking), the map never appears. When an `activeBooking` exists, a map is present inside the booking/tracking interface, in `UserDashboard`. I\'ve confirmed the map removal, as it is only present in tracking and operator states.\n\n\n**Confirming Route Visualization**\n\nNow I\'m confirming that the map visualizes the ambulance route dynamically. The goal is a clear visual representation of the ambulance\'s progress in real-time, focusing on accurate updates to vehicle position and route display. I am also investigating the demo reset flow to eliminate a potential source of errors. I\'ll focus on the data updates to the `routePolyline` prop.\n\n\n"
