  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Ambulance Dispatch**\n\nI\'ve realized the current implementation in `App.tsx` directly dispatches the ambulance as \"en\\_route\\_pickup\". This contradicts Requirement 4, which requires showing the pickup location initially and only displaying the ambulance route after operator acceptance. It looks like the immediate dispatch is not aligned with the requirements.\n\n\n**Refining Booking Stages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how booking stages and map updates will work. My plan is that `handleCreateBooking` will start bookings as \'pending\', with `assignedUnitId` and `routePolyline` undefined. The map will initially center on the pickup location with a marker in scanning mode. Once `handleAcceptBooking` is called, route calculations happen, the booking transitions to \'en\\_route\\_pickup\', and both the map and ambulance status update accordingly. I\'m considering dynamic route and position updates through further trip stages.\n\n\n"
