  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Bookings Initialization**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how `bookings` is initialized in `App.tsx`. I\'ve made changes to ensure a clean setup.  Specifically, I\'m working on robustly handling the retrieval from local storage, making sure to gracefully manage any potential errors or empty states, and ensuring that the default state is handled correctly.\n\n\n**Improving Booking Submission**\n\nI\'ve been working on preventing duplicate booking submissions. I\'ve implemented `isSubmittingRef` and `isSubmitting` state variables to control the flow and prevent rapid clicks. The updated `handleCreateBooking` function now checks for an existing active booking before proceeding, and sets a submission lock to prevent accidental multiple submissions. This should dramatically improve reliability.\n\n\n**Generating Booking Metadata**\n\nI\'m now generating the metadata for new bookings. I\'m focusing on creating unique `id` and `trackingCode` values using `Date.now()` and random number generation, respectively.  I\'ve incorporated the patient and location details from the input and derived the `stage` as \'pending\' initially.  I\'m also including placeholders for things like `assignedUnitId` and route details.\n\n\n**Finalizing Booking Data Transmission**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new booking data with the backend. I am making use of the data that I\'ve assembled to POST a request to `/api/bookings`. The request body includes patient and location details, equipment requested, and booking type. Additionally, I am managing the \'pending\' stage. I am also making sure that the toast and `isSubmittingRef` are handled correctly at the end.\n\n\n**Refining Booking Acceptance**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `handleAcceptBooking` function, particularly the logic for assigning ambulances. I\'m prioritizing finding the nearest available ambulance using `findNearestAvailableAmbulance`. I\'m also fetching the first phase of the road route, from ambulance to the patient pickup, by using the `getDrivingRoute` to populate `phase1Polyline`. I\'m handling the cases where route data retrieval might fail. Additionally, I am calculating and including `dispatchDistKm` and `dispatchEtaMins`.\n\n\n**Updating Booking Progress**\n\nI\'m now integrating the route data into both the ambulances and booking states following an acceptance. Specifically, I\'m updating the `bookings` state to reflect the route polyline, distance, ETA, and the ambulance\'s current position. I am also adjusting the ambulance state by setting the status to \'en_route_pickup\' and associating the booking\'s `id`. This will update the map with the new route.\n\n\n**Integrating Booking Updates**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on the backend updates following ambulance assignment, especially updating the booking stage to `en_route_pickup`. I\'m working on how this information is transmitted to the server with `fetch` and handle potential errors. I\'ve also incorporated a toast message confirming the dispatch details, specifically the ambulance callsign, station, and ETA. I\'m also ensuring that the booking and ambulance statuses are accurately updated, including recording acceptance and dispatch timestamps.\n\n\n**Visualizing Map Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Leaflet map component with the application\'s state. I\'m focusing on dynamically updating map markers for pickups, dropoffs, and ambulances, as well as drawing the route polyline. I am coordinating the display based on active booking data, including stage-specific indicators. I\'m also ensuring that route recalculation is triggered correctly when needed.\n\n\n**Enhancing Driver View**\n\nI\'m now integrating a conditional display for the driver view. I\'m incorporating the `OpenDriverView` function to render the driver interface. I\'m also ensuring the 3D viewer is toggled correctly using `setIs3DViewerOpen`.  The focus is providing a direct link to the driver view, as needed.\n\n\n"
