  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Dashboard**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `src/components/UserDashboard/UserDashboard.tsx`. I\'ve added `LeafletMap` and `Radio` imports. Further updates include component integration within the User Dashboard. I\'m moving toward incorporating a map and radio button functionality. The goal is to provide a user-friendly interface.\n\n\n**Implementing Active Booking Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating auto-accept functionality for pending bookings, simulating an operator\'s action. I\'ve introduced a countdown and a \"\342\232\241 Accept Dispatch\" button to skip the timer. When active, I\'m rendering an active booking and tracking view, ensuring the necessary props are available for this section. I\'m focusing on handling different booking stages within the user dashboard.\n\n\n**Visualizing Route Information**\n\nI\'m now integrating an interactive Leaflet map within the user dashboard to enhance the active booking view. The map will display pickup and drop-off coordinates, ambulance locations, and route polylines. I\'m incorporating the ability to handle route recalculation, accuracy details, and potential route errors. This will provide users with a real-time, visual overview of the trip.\n\n\n**Developing Booking Telemetry**\n\nI\'m currently working on displaying key active booking information, including live ETA, road distance, and dispatched unit details, dynamically updating based on the booking stage. I\'m focusing on rendering a telemetry strip with the estimated data, driver details if available, and a clickable stage progression stepper. I\'m ensuring each stage is correctly represented within the user interface.\n\n\n**Designing Homepage Elements**\n\nI\'m now designing the homepage elements for when there isn\'t an active booking. I\'m focusing on the \"Emergency Dispatch Hero\" section, including the Delhi NCR badge, title, and subtitle. I\'m prioritizing GPS pickup status with a \"Detect My GPS\" button, displaying the detected address and accuracy, with a graceful error fallback. The core will be a 5-second hold-to-confirm button with a pulsing ring, and a manual booking option.\n\n\n"
