  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Component Imports**\n\nI\'m currently updating the imports in `UserDashboard.tsx`. I\'ve added various types like `Booking`, `Hospital`, and `PatientProfile`. I\'m also including `LatLng`, and `AmbulanceUnit`, so that the component can properly render the needed information. I\'ve updated the `UserDashboardProps` to reflect these changes.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Context**\n\nI\'ve significantly expanded the imports in `UserDashboard.tsx`. Now included are `BookingDocument`, `TripStage`, plus mock data like `HOSPITALS`, `LANDMARKS`, and `EQUIPMENT_CATALOG`. I\'ve imported several React components, such as `HoldToConfirmButton`, `HospitalDirectory`, and `LeafletMap`. I\'ve integrated many lucide-react icons, and updated `UserDashboardProps` for new contextual data.\n\n\n**Defining Dashboard Callbacks**\n\nI\'m now integrating critical callback functions within `UserDashboardProps`, including `onDetectGPS`, `onSubmitBooking`, and `onCancelActiveBooking`. I\'m handling the logic for GPS status, and defining booking actions, along with updating types for the `patientProfile`. I\'ve added a few more, `onOpenUploadModal`, `onOpen3DModal`, `onRecalculateRoute`, `onAcceptBooking`, and `onAdvanceStage`. I\'m including props for ambulance data, route information, and submission states.\n\n\n**Implementing Auto-Accept Logic**\n\nI\'ve just added an `useEffect` hook to implement auto-accept functionality for bookings. A timer begins when a booking enters a `\'pending\'` state, decrementing `autoAcceptSeconds`. Upon reaching zero, or when a user simulates accepting the booking, `onAcceptBooking` is triggered. I\'m making sure to handle the cleanup using `clearInterval` to prevent memory leaks and ensure precise timing.\n\n\n**Analyzing Dispatch UI**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on the UI rendering logic within the `UserDashboard` component, specifically lines 177 to 656, pertaining to the \'dispatch\' tab. I\'m verifying the conditional rendering based on `activeBooking` and `activeTab`. If there\'s an active booking, and it\'s not completed or cancelled, I\'ll render the interactive map and the booking details. Otherwise, I\'ll display the homepage components: the hold button, GPS status, manual booking options, hospital network preview, and emergency helpline information \342\200\223 but importantly, *no* map until a booking is active.\n\n\n"
