    thinking: "**Analyzing Conditional Rendering**\n\nI\'ve been examining the conditional rendering logic, specifically lines 191-310. It appears that when a booking is active and not completed or cancelled, it renders a tracking card and then proceeds to the emergency booking hero. My focus is on the impact of this particular `if` statement.\n\n\n**Refining Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now shifting gears to the component structure within the \'dispatch\' tab, specifically lines 647 onwards. My objective is to modularize the Hospital Directory Section and the Emergency Dispatch Tab to be their own components, instead of a mishmash of the two. This refactoring aims to improve maintainability.\n\n\n**Interpreting Booking Stages**\n\nI\'m currently delving into the implications of `activeBooking.stage` within the conditional rendering. I\'m focusing on how the different stage values (\'pending\', \'dispatched\', etc.) affect the display of ambulance details and request status messages. This stage dictates the text and visual cues presented to the user, like the use of the radio icon and its associated animation. I\'m attempting to clarify the logic.\n\n\n**Clarifying UI States**\n\nI\'m now examining how the `activeBooking.stage` value influences the user interface\'s visual presentation. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the visual states for different booking stages; For example, when the booking is pending the button is made available. It\'s key to identify all possible states, and how they correspond to UI elements.\n\n\n**Evaluating Button Functionality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the \'dispatch\' tab, specifically the actions available when an ambulance is requested. I\'m assessing the impact of the \'Accept Dispatch\', \'Share Trip Link\', and \'Cancel Request\' buttons, and their states at the time. My goal is to determine the complete state of the workflow and available states to the operator.\n\n\n**Interpreting Pending State**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"pending\" stage, specifically the UI it produces. It\'s clear the design shows an active ambulance search with a blinking indicator and a specific message to the user. I\'m exploring the nuances of the display elements, like the amber color palette and the fleet unit detail.\n\n\n**Assessing Connection Display**\n\nI\'m now examining the auto-connect indicator logic in more detail, specifically how the countdown timer interacts with the map view. I need to understand how the countdown and map work together within the \'Tracking Interface\' section.\n\n\n**Investigating UI Updates**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implications of the real-time telemetry strip. Specifically, I\'m examining the ETA display and how it updates based on the active booking stage. I\'m focusing on the condition where the display changes from showing an approximate ETA to a more specific numerical ETA, as well as the design elements.\n\n\n**Interpreting Dynamic Distances**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on how the UI dynamically displays distance. I see that the distance displayed varies according to the `activeBooking.stage`. Specifically, I\'m examining how the text changes between a tilde value and a direct numerical value, based on whether the booking stage is pending or not. I\'m also examining the nuances of what is displayed for the dispatched unit.\n\n\n**Evaluating Ambulance Information**\n\nI\'m now examining how ambulance information is rendered, specifically the hospital-stationed indicator and destination details. I\'m focusing on the display of station names and the truncation of the drop-off address. The visual cues, such as the hospital or police car icons, are also under scrutiny.\n\n\n**Interpreting Ambulance Details**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the rendering of ambulance driver details. Specifically, I\'m examining how the driver\'s photo, name, rating, and paramedic details are displayed. I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy and information density to see if it efficiently presents key information. Also, I\'m looking at the direct call functionality.\n\n\n**Examining UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now investigating specific UI elements related to the ambulance display. I\'m focusing on the \"Direct Driver Call\" button, and the \"3D Ambulance Telemetry\" button. Specifically, I\'m examining their state and their relationship within the overall dispatch workflow. I\'m focusing on how the buttons look, function, and when they are available.\n\n\n**Analyzing Booking Stages**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual progress indicator that displays the booking stage. I\'m assessing the progression of each step within the dispatch workflow, going through \'pending\', \'accepted\', and onward to \'completed.\' My objective is to determine how the UI reflects each distinct stage. I\'m evaluating the step number and associated text labels.\n\n\n**Interpreting Workflow Steps**\n\nI\'m now deeply examining the visual representation of the dispatch workflow\'s progress indicator. I\'m focused on how UI elements visually represent each stage. I\'m analyzing the styling applied to each step, particularly the \"pending\", \"accepted\", \"en\\_route\\_pickup\", stages and how they relate to the progression logic using an array. I\'m focusing on UI elements and their visual cues, such as the checkmark, and current stage highlighting.\n\n\n**Evaluating Route Displays**\n\nI\'m now examining how route details are rendered, focusing on `pickupAddress` within the progress indicator. Specifically, I\'m analyzing how these details are formatted, and what is displayed. I\'m reviewing how the data is handled within the context of the dispatch workflow\'s stage indicator.\n\n\n**Interpreting Dropoff Address**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the dynamic display of the dropoff address within the UI. I\'m reviewing how `activeBooking.dropoffAddress` is rendered and formatted within a specific component. I\'m examining its relationship to nearby UI components and its styling. Also, I\'m examining how its relation with patient details.\n\n\n**Analyzing Equipment Catalog**\n\nI\'m now examining how equipment catalog items are rendered within the emergency booking hero. I\'m focusing on the display of equipment names based on their IDs from `EQUIPMENT_CATALOG`, and how the UI handles cases where the ID isn\'t found. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the styling of the equipment labels, and how the values are displayed.\n\n\n**Interpreting Hero Content**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the hero section content, specifically the title, subtitle, and description. I\'m focusing on how this section will be displayed and how it will influence the user\'s perception of the emergency dispatch workflow. I\'m focusing on the relationship of the content in this section.\n\nI\'m focusing on the error handling section and reviewing its components.\n\n\n**Examining Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now diving into the error handling components, specifically regarding location permissions and GPS errors. I\'m focusing on the visual cues, such as the amber color palette and the \"Retry GPS Detection\" button. Also, I\'m analyzing how the UI communicates the issue and offers a solution to the user, particularly when an address is involved.\n\n\n\n**Interpreting GPS Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the GPS coordinate display, particularly the interaction between the `Crosshair` icon and the accompanying text. I\'m focusing on the \"Detecting GPS coordinates...\" state and how it affects the visual cue using `animate-spin`. Also, I\'m examining how the first element of the address is rendered for the operator\'s benefit.\n\n\n**Assessing UI Interactions**\n\nI\'m now examining the \"Refresh GPS\" button and its relationship with the \"Locating...\" text, specifically the `isDetectingGPS` flag. I am also looking at the impact of the hold-to-confirm button and it is state with the current booking stage. Also, I am evaluating the impact and function of `onDetectGPS`. Finally, I\'m examining what would happen if the state changes.\n\n\n**Evaluating Booking Details**\n\nI\'m now examining the \"Manual Booking\" toggle button, assessing the visual cues indicating its active state. I\'m reviewing the transition between the regular and selected states, focusing on the styling change and the associated icon updates. This will allow for enhanced ease of use within the user\'s workflow.\n\n\n**Refining Manual Booking**\n\nI\'m now examining the \"Manual Booking\" toggle button\'s associated content within the UI. I\'m focusing on the visual grouping of custom hospital selection and related details. I\'m assessing the impact of this section on the overall flow, specifically how it contributes to the emergency dispatch workflow.\n\n\n"
