  planner_response {
    response: "The DropAid application has been updated to remove the map from the homepage and display it exclusively after an ambulance booking is initiated.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Homepage Map Removal:**\n   - Completely removed the map from the homepage.\n   - The homepage now presents a focused emergency booking experience: the 5-second Hold-to-Confirm emergency button, real-time GPS location badge, manual booking configuration drawer, and verified hospital network directory.\n\n2. **Map Display on Booking Initiation:**\n   - Both booking methods\342\200\224holding the red button for 5 seconds or submitting the manual booking form\342\200\224transition directly into the unified Active Booking & Tracking interface.\n   - The interactive Leaflet map opens immediately within this tracking view and remains accessible throughout the entire trip.\n\n3. **Accurate Location & Centering:**\n   - Automatically centers the map on the user\'s verified GPS pickup location (or their selected manual pickup landmark).\n   - Renders the patient pickup marker with GPS accuracy bounds, destination hospital ER marker, assigned ambulance with sirens, and driving road routes.\n   - Added automatic tile invalidation on mount to guarantee crisp rendering without gray edges.\n\n4. **Dynamic Dispatch & Multi-Stage Tracking:**\n   - **Initial Search State (`pending`):** Displays the pickup location with an active radar search aura and a status banner indicating fleet scanning across Delhi NCR. Includes an auto-dispatch countdown and an instant *\"Accept Dispatch (Simulate Operator)\"* trigger.\n   - **Operator Acceptance:** Assigns the nearest available unit, computes the driving road route, renders the ambulance marker, and animates the vehicle along the road coordinates toward the patient.\n   - **Trip Progression:** Dynamically updates routes and telemetry through all stages (*En Route*, *On Scene*, *Transporting to ER*, *Hospital Arrival*, and *Completed*).\n   - **Trip Completion/Cancellation:** Frees the vehicle, archives the record into Trip History, and returns the user to the clean homepage without the map."
    thinking: "**Verifying Instruction Adherence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the first instruction: removing the map from the homepage. The goal is to create a cleaner, more professional landing page, centered on ambulance services. My next step will be to verify the map is fully and effectively gone.\n\n\n**Confirming Booking Display**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the homepage, on initial load and with no active booking, only shows the booking interface; the map is gone. Furthermore, I\'ve verified that the interactive map only appears after a user initiates a booking, either via the 5-second hold or a manual form. Once this occurs, the map loads in the booking view.\n\n\n**Assessing Map Functionality**\n\nI\'ve examined the map\'s current functionality, focusing on dynamic tracking. I\'ve verified the pickup location display and ambulance search status initially. I\'ve also confirmed that upon dispatch acceptance, the map updates to display the assigned ambulance, its calculated route, and animated marker movement, which will follow road coordinates. I\'ve validated destination marker, assigned ambulance, and road-following route display.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The DropAid application has been updated to remove the map from the homepage and display it exclusively after an ambulance booking is initiated.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Homepage Map Removal:**\n   - Completely removed the map from the homepage.\n   - The homepage now presents a focused emergency booking experience: the 5-second Hold-to-Confirm emergency button, real-time GPS location badge, manual booking configuration drawer, and verified hospital network directory.\n\n2. **Map Display on Booking Initiation:**\n   - Both booking methods\342\200\224holding the red button for 5 seconds or submitting the manual booking form\342\200\224transition directly into the unified Active Booking & Tracking interface.\n   - The interactive Leaflet map opens immediately within this tracking view and remains accessible throughout the entire trip.\n\n3. **Accurate Location & Centering:**\n   - Automatically centers the map on the user\'s verified GPS pickup location (or their selected manual pickup landmark).\n   - Renders the patient pickup marker with GPS accuracy bounds, destination hospital ER marker, assigned ambulance with sirens, and driving road routes.\n   - Added automatic tile invalidation on mount to guarantee crisp rendering without gray edges.\n\n4. **Dynamic Dispatch & Multi-Stage Tracking:**\n   - **Initial Search State (`pending`):** Displays the pickup location with an active radar search aura and a status banner indicating fleet scanning across Delhi NCR. Includes an auto-dispatch countdown and an instant *\"Accept Dispatch (Simulate Operator)\"* trigger.\n   - **Operator Acceptance:** Assigns the nearest available unit, computes the driving road route, renders the ambulance marker, and animates the vehicle along the road coordinates toward the patient.\n   - **Trip Progression:** Dynamically updates routes and telemetry through all stages (*En Route*, *On Scene*, *Transporting to ER*, *Hospital Arrival*, and *Completed*).\n   - **Trip Completion/Cancellation:** Frees the vehicle, archives the record into Trip History, and returns the user to the clean homepage without the map."
