  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Fixes Meticulously**\n\nI\'m pleased with `getDrivingRoute`; it\'s consistently reliable, even handling OSRM timeouts with its backup using `generateRealisticRoadRoute`. This generates plausible routes with realistic block turns. Now, I\'m carefully examining the required corrections for this.\n\n\n**Implementing Transport Routing**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress addressing routing after patient pickup. Upon a \"Patient Picked Up\" status change, the old pickup route is immediately removed, and a new road-following route to the hospital is requested. Routing failures are now handled with a retry option and a clear error message. I\'m also updating destination markers and the polyline, ETA, distance, and navigation instructions on the Leaflet map.\n\n\n**Enhancing Arrival Indicators**\n\nI\'m now integrating dynamic feedback for the ER arrival target. I plan to use `stage`, `isTransporting`, or `activeBooking?.stage` to trigger a pulsating or highlighting effect on the ER marker in `LeafletMap`. I\'ve updated `UserDashboard.tsx` to handle route updates more responsively, ensuring immediate polyline rendering and dynamic updates of ETA and distance based on `routeEtaMins` and `routeDistanceKm`. I\'m also adding a retry button on the map if the hospital route fetch encounters an error. Finally, I\'m updating the `driver_cockpit` view in `OperatorDashboard.tsx` to display specific transport instructions when the stage is \'transporting.\'\n\n\n**Synchronizing Route Updates**\n\nI\'m focusing on seamless route synchronization between user and operator views, ensuring consistent data. Upon patient pickup, I\'m clearing the old route polyline and resetting the waypoint index. The animation now starts from the driver\'s pickup position along the new hospital route\'s coordinates. I\'m prioritizing the animation to use only the freshest coordinates. I\'m also ensuring the operator view also gets the new route details such as polyline and distance information.\n\n\n**Addressing Route Synchronization**\n\nI\'m now synchronizing hospital route data: polyline, distance, and ETA with the `bookings` state. I\'ve updated the `/api/bookings/:id/stage` endpoint to accept and handle these values in the request body, reflecting them in the `serverBookings` data.\nI\'m also working to prevent race conditions during routing requests. I\'m using `routingRequestIdRef` to manage asynchronous responses, ensuring that only the most recent routing data is used. Finally, I have implemented a mechanism to clear error states and present a retry option when `getDrivingRoute` encounters issues.\n\n\n"
