  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying UI Language**\n\nI\'m focusing on the UI label for the \"transporting\" stage in `types/index.ts`. I want the UI to clearly convey \"Patient Picked Up \342\200\224 En Route to Hospital ER\" to avoid any confusion.\n\n\n**Defining Route Logic**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the `handleAdvanceStage` function, specifically when the stage transitions to \"transporting.\" My focus is on the sequence: the immediate clearance of the old route, resetting waypoints, setting route polyline to empty array, and clearing the map. Crucially, I\'m working on pinpointing the origin of the new route\342\200\224is it the ambulance\'s last known location or the patient\'s pickup coordinates? Plus, I\'m thinking about how to prevent race conditions during routing requests with a new ref.\n\n\n**Implementing Route Error Handling**\n\nI\'ve just added detailed error handling to the routing logic. If `getDrivingRoute` fails, I\'m now clearing the polyline, setting an error message, and providing a retry function for the user. On success, I\342\200\231m updating the route polyline, distance, ETA, and ambulance/booking states with the route details. Crucially, I\'m incrementing a routing request ID, and checking for stale responses to prevent race conditions.\n\n\n**Updating Transport Display**\n\nI\'m now incorporating stage update data to be sent to the server. I will include the polyline, distance, and ETA. I will also incorporate Leaflet updates to show the pickup marker as complete and the hospital marker with an active pulsating ring during the transporting stage. Additionally, the map will immediately fit the bounds of the new route.\n\n\n**Refining Dashboard Displays**\n\nI\'m currently updating the `UserDashboard` component. I\'ve passed the `routePolyline` directly to the `LeafletMap`. I\'m focusing on the telemetry strip, where I\'m displaying the live ETA and road distance, using `activeBooking` data when available or fallback data. For \"transporting\" stages, I\'m displaying the clear status \"Patient Picked Up \302\267 Priority Transit to ER\" and ensuring the destination bay clearly shows the Hospital ER. The stepper now reflects \"5. Patient Picked Up (Transporting),\" and I\'m adding a \"Simulate: Patient Picked Up\" button when the booking is \"on_scene.\"\n\n\n"
