  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Icon Updates**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `LeafletMap.tsx` component and noticed a critical detail regarding the `dropoffMarkerRef`. It seems that the `setIcon(...)` method wasn\'t being called when `dropoffMarkerRef.current` was available. This means that dynamically updating the `dropoffIcon` based on the `tripStage` (specifically when it\'s \'transporting\') necessitates invoking `dropoffMarkerRef.current.setIcon(dropoffIcon)`. This omission explains a previous bug.\n\n\n**Refining Icon Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing dynamic icon updates for both pickup and dropoff markers based on the `tripStage`. When `tripStage` is \'transporting\', the pickup icon changes to \"\342\234\223 PATIENT PICKED UP\" in emerald, while the dropoff icon becomes \"\360\237\232\250 EMERGENCY HOSPITAL ER\" with a pulsing siren ring. I\'m also ensuring the route polyline color adjusts based on the trip stage; Rose red for emergency transport and sky blue for other states.\n\n\n**Optimizing Route Rendering**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough in how routes are rendered. When `tripStage` changes to \'transporting\', the polyline is effectively removed and set to null. Then, upon recalculating the hospital route, the new polyline is added. This ensures a clean transition without stale routes or jarring visuals. I\'m also examining the handling of rapid \"Advance to next stage\" clicks and how `routingRequestIdRef` is used to manage route requests.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_16463"
      name: "view_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"AbsolutePath\":\"/src/App.tsx\", \"EndLine\":380, \"StartLine\":265, \"toolAction\":\"Viewing handleAdvanceStage in App.tsx\", \"toolSummary\":\"View handleAdvanceStage in App.tsx\"}"
