  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing App.tsx Structure**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting `src/App.tsx`, aiming to overhaul the stage transition and routing. The goal is complete alignment with all six project requirements. My focus is now the immediate removal of previous pickup routes. I\'m exploring how the existing structure can be adapted to ensure this is handled efficiently and seamlessly.\n\n\n**Implementing Transport Transition**\n\nI\'ve finalized the logic for the stage transition to \'transporting\'. When `nextStage` is \'transporting\', I immediately clear the route polyline and waypoint index, reset any route errors, and update the booking and ambulance status accordingly. Also, the ambulance will have a road-following route generated to the hospital using `getDrivingRoute` with OSRM and waypoint bends. Finally, I\'ve implemented a race condition prevention system using `routingRequestIdRef` to handle route updates.\n\n\n**Finalizing Road Coordinates**\n\nI\'ve integrated the hospital route data by updating route properties within the `bookings` state. Specifically, the route\'s polyline, distance, and ETA are all updated. I\'ve also implemented the API call to persist the stage change on the backend. In the operator view map, I pass the trip stage and route polyline as props. Next, the ambulance\'s animation will be sequenced according to the actual road coordinates from the new route\'s polyline.\n\n\n"
