  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Routing Logic**\n\nI\'ve been working on the routing logic and decided to declare `routingRequestIdRef` and `isSubmittingRef` using `useRef`. I\'m starting to design the `handleAdvanceStage` and route transition logic, particularly for when `nextStage` is \'transporting\'. I want to ensure this works optimally.\n\n\n**Implementing Immediate State Updates**\n\nI\'ve decided to prioritize immediate UI updates when transitioning to the \'transporting\' stage. This involves clearing the existing route polyline and resetting waypoint animations to avoid stale data. I\'m also ensuring the booking stage and ambulance status reflect the transition instantly, including setting the ambulance speed. I\'m now requesting the new road-following route based on the ambulance\'s current location to ensure the map renders correctly.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Route Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the hospital route data updates directly into the booking state. I\'m focusing on ensuring data consistency between the rendered route polyline, distance, ETA, and the booking details themselves, including the vehicle\'s current position. I\'m using a `reqId` check to prevent race conditions and ensure only the latest route data is used. I\'m carefully managing `waypointIndexRef` as well.\n\n\n**Updating Backend Synchronization**\n\nI\'ve just added the crucial server synchronization. After calculating the hospital route and transitioning to the \'transporting\' stage, I\'m now sending the updated route data, including the polyline, distance, and ETA, to the backend server. I\'m also including the assigned unit ID. I\'m handling potential network errors with a background sync strategy. Finally, I\'m displaying a toast message to inform the user of the patient\'s transport status.\n\n\n**Handling Scene Arrival**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the implications of `nextStage` being \'on_scene\'. I\'m clearing the route and resetting the waypoint index. I\'m also ensuring the ambulance status correctly updates to \'on_scene\', its location matches the pickup coords, and its speed is set to zero. This includes updating both the ambulance state and the booking state to reflect the transition accurately.\n\n\n**Finalizing Hospital Arrival**\n\nI\'m now implementing the logic for when the ambulance arrives at the hospital. I\'m resetting the route and updating both ambulance and booking states to reflect the arrival. I\'m setting the ambulance status to \'at_hospital\', its location to the dropoff coordinates, and its speed to zero. I\'m also updating the booking stage to \'at_hospital\', clearing the route polyline, and setting the `currentVehiclePosition` and `arrivedHospital` timestamp. I\'m addressing the retry route behavior to recalculate routes in either case.\n\n\n**Calculating Hospital Route**\n\nI\'m now recalculating the hospital route when handling a `retry` scenario. I\'m focusing on ensuring data consistency by updating both the route state variables and the booking state with the new polyline, distance, and ETA. I\'m also using the latest route data and waypoint index and handling errors gracefully by updating the state. I\'m ensuring the data integrity is sound to ensure a smooth user experience.\n\n\n**Calculating Pickup Route**\n\nI\'m now focusing on calculating the route to the pickup location when the booking stage is \'en_route_pickup\'. I am ensuring that the route calculation logic works as expected. I\'m prioritizing getting the route with the right data to ensure the map renders correctly to display the ambulance\'s route to the patient. I\'m handling potential errors to maintain a seamless user experience. I have handled race conditions.\n\n\n**Verifying Route Calculation**\n\nI\'m now verifying the route calculation process. Specifically, I\'m checking the `calculateCurrentRoute` function to confirm it correctly tracks the `routingRequestIdRef` and to ensure that `handleRetryRoute` in `UserDashboard` also gets `onRecalculateRoute` to keep the data consistent. This ensures the route calculations work as expected with the current data.\n\n\n"
