  }
  planner_response {
    response: "The ambulance route transition bug has been resolved with complete multi-view synchronization, immediate layer clearance, and race condition prevention:\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Immediate Route Removal on Patient Pickup (`transporting`)**:\n   - As soon as the trip advances to **\"Patient Picked Up\"** (`transporting`), the previous Phase 1 pickup route layer is immediately removed from the map and `waypointIndexRef` is reset to 0 before the hospital route calculation finishes.\n   - Synchronously clears stale polyline coordinates in both the active booking object and global routing state to prevent route shadowing.\n\n2. **Road-Following Hospital ER Route**:\n   - Generates a new driving route originating directly from the ambulance\342\200\231s current scene location to the selected hospital emergency bay.\n   - Employs OSRM with realistic block-following grid waypoint fallback (no straight lines or stale pickup coordinates).\n   - Dynamically updates road distance and live ETA to the hospital destination bay.\n\n3. **Destination Marker & UI Updates**:\n   - **Pickup Marker**: Updates to `\342\234\223 PATIENT PICKED UP (SCENE CLEAR)` with green completion styling and disabled dragging once patient pickup occurs.\n   - **Hospital Marker**: Activates a pulsing emergency ER beacon (`\360\237\232\250 DESTINATION ER BAY`) and automatically reframes map bounds to comfortably encompass the vehicle and hospital destination.\n   - **Driver Cockpit & Navigation**: Dynamic turn cues transition to priority hospital transport (`PRIORITY ER CORRIDOR` with patient-on-board siren speed telemetry).\n\n4. **Race Condition Prevention & Error Recovery**:\n   - Added request ID tracking (`routingRequestIdRef`) to discard out-of-order routing responses during rapid stage clicks.\n   - If network routing fails, a clear retry notice is displayed on the map HUD and tracking banner (`Retry Hospital Route`) rather than retaining misleading stale paths.\n\n5. **Full State Synchronization**:\n   - Persists updated Phase 2 polyline, distance, and ETA across `/api/bookings/:id/stage` and client local storage, keeping both User and Operator dashboards in lockstep."
    modified_response: "The ambulance route transition bug has been resolved with complete multi-view synchronization, immediate layer clearance, and race condition prevention:\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Immediate Route Removal on Patient Pickup (`transporting`)**:\n   - As soon as the trip advances to **\"Patient Picked Up\"** (`transporting`), the previous Phase 1 pickup route layer is immediately removed from the map and `waypointIndexRef` is reset to 0 before the hospital route calculation finishes.\n   - Synchronously clears stale polyline coordinates in both the active booking object and global routing state to prevent route shadowing.\n\n2. **Road-Following Hospital ER Route**:\n   - Generates a new driving route originating directly from the ambulance\342\200\231s current scene location to the selected hospital emergency bay.\n   - Employs OSRM with realistic block-following grid waypoint fallback (no straight lines or stale pickup coordinates).\n   - Dynamically updates road distance and live ETA to the hospital destination bay.\n\n3. **Destination Marker & UI Updates**:\n   - **Pickup Marker**: Updates to `\342\234\223 PATIENT PICKED UP (SCENE CLEAR)` with green completion styling and disabled dragging once patient pickup occurs.\n   - **Hospital Marker**: Activates a pulsing emergency ER beacon (`\360\237\232\250 DESTINATION ER BAY`) and automatically reframes map bounds to comfortably encompass the vehicle and hospital destination.\n   - **Driver Cockpit & Navigation**: Dynamic turn cues transition to priority hospital transport (`PRIORITY ER CORRIDOR` with patient-on-board siren speed telemetry).\n\n4. **Race Condition Prevention & Error Recovery**:\n   - Added request ID tracking (`routingRequestIdRef`) to discard out-of-order routing responses during rapid stage clicks.\n   - If network routing fails, a clear retry notice is displayed on the map HUD and tracking banner (`Retry Hospital Route`) rather than retaining misleading stale paths.\n\n5. **Full State Synchronization**:\n   - Persists updated Phase 2 polyline, distance, and ETA across `/api/bookings/:id/stage` and client local storage, keeping both User and Operator dashboards in lockstep."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
