  user_input {
    user_response: "Update the existing DropAid application. Fix the following issues without rebuilding the app or breaking working features.\n\n**1. Separate User and Operator Controls**\n- Remove all operator-only tools from the User Panel, including time skip, trip-stage simulation buttons, manual status controls, and reset controls.\n- Keep these tools exclusively in the Operator Panel or Demo Controls.\n- Ensure users can only access customer-facing booking and tracking features.\n\n**2. Lock Locations After Booking**\n- Before booking confirmation, allow users to edit pickup and destination locations.\n- Once a booking is submitted, lock both locations and prevent changes from the User Panel.\n- Display the confirmed pickup and destination as read-only.\n- Allow location changes only through an authorized operator workflow, with route recalculation and synchronized updates.\n\n**3. Restrict Cancellation After Pickup**\n- Allow users to cancel an eligible booking before the driver confirms patient pickup.\n- Once the patient is picked up, disable user cancellation and hide or remove the cancellation action.\n- Display a clear message: \"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\"\n- Enforce these rules in the booking logic, not just by hiding the button.\n\n**4. Remove Navbar Logo**\n- Remove the DropAid logo/icon from the navigation bar while preserving the DropAid text branding, alignment, and responsive layout.\n\n**Quality Control:** Test user and operator permissions, location locking, cancellation before and after pickup, route synchronization, and mobile responsiveness. Prevent unauthorized state changes, stale data, and duplicate actions. Fix all console errors and verify existing booking and tracking workflows still function correctly."
    items {
      text: "Update the existing DropAid application. Fix the following issues without rebuilding the app or breaking working features.\n\n**1. Separate User and Operator Controls**\n- Remove all operator-only tools from the User Panel, including time skip, trip-stage simulation buttons, manual status controls, and reset controls.\n- Keep these tools exclusively in the Operator Panel or Demo Controls.\n- Ensure users can only access customer-facing booking and tracking features.\n\n**2. Lock Locations After Booking**\n- Before booking confirmation, allow users to edit pickup and destination locations.\n- Once a booking is submitted, lock both locations and prevent changes from the User Panel.\n- Display the confirmed pickup and destination as read-only.\n- Allow location changes only through an authorized operator workflow, with route recalculation and synchronized updates.\n\n**3. Restrict Cancellation After Pickup**\n- Allow users to cancel an eligible booking before the driver confirms patient pickup.\n- Once the patient is picked up, disable user cancellation and hide or remove the cancellation action.\n- Display a clear message: \"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\"\n- Enforce these rules in the booking logic, not just by hiding the button.\n\n**4. Remove Navbar Logo**\n- Remove the DropAid logo/icon from the navigation bar while preserving the DropAid text branding, alignment, and responsive layout.\n\n**Quality Control:** Test user and operator permissions, location locking, cancellation before and after pickup, route synchronization, and mobile responsiveness. Prevent unauthorized state changes, stale data, and duplicate actions. Fix all console errors and verify existing booking and tracking workflows still function correctly."
    }
  }
}
