  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Requirements in Detail**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the project requirements. I\'m starting with a detailed analysis of Requirement 1, the separation of user and operator controls. This involves removing all operator-specific tools from the User Panel. I am also planning the design and implementation of new operator controls. I have a detailed plan to start.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on cleaning up the `UserDashboard.tsx` component. I\'ve removed the `autoAcceptSeconds` countdown and the auto-accept functionality, ensuring bookings now stay in a \"pending\" state until operator acceptance. The simulation buttons have also been removed to meet user requirements. I\'m double-checking the file for any remaining operator controls.\n\n\n**Implementing Location Locking**\n\nNow I\'m tackling the location locking requirement. I\'m focusing on preventing changes to pickup and destination locations once a booking is active. I\'ve disabled marker dragging and removed drag cursors when the booking is active, specifically in `LeafletMap.tsx`. I\'m also addressing the landmark popups to disable location changes once the booking is in place.\n\n\n**Designing Location Lockdown Interface**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI for location locking during active trips. Buttons for location changes will be hidden or replaced with a \"Locations locked\" message. Confirmed pickup and destination will be read-only cards, and Hospital Directory options will be disabled with an explanation message. Next, I\'ll build the operator reroute feature, starting with the `OperatorDashboard.tsx` changes. I also plan to add an \"Operator Reroute\" feature!\n\n\n**Defining Rerouting Logic**\n\nI\'m now outlining the steps for operator rerouting. When the operator adjusts the destination or pickup location, I\'ll trigger an `onOperatorUpdateLocation` handler. This will recalculate the driving route and update the state and server. I\'m planning to synchronize these changes across the `LeafletMap`, User Panel, and Operator Panel, displaying a toast notification to keep everyone informed.\n\n**Implementing Booking Cancellation Restrictions**\n\nI\'m now tackling the user cancellation restrictions. I\'m allowing cancellations at stages `pending`, `accepted`, `en_route_pickup`, and `on_scene`. After pickup, I\'ll disable the cancellation button and display a clear message in the User panel to indicate this restriction.\n\n\n**Finalizing UI Messaging**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final UI elements and enforcing the new cancellation rules. I\'m adding a prominent message to the user panel: \"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\" Crucially, I\'ve included a direct operator contact link using a `tel:` link. I\'ve also strengthened the booking logic to enforce these rules, handling cancellation restrictions in both `App.tsx` and the `server.ts` routes. The logic rejects user-initiated cancellation requests after the `en_route_pickup` or `on_scene` stages. I\'m now testing these updates to ensure seamless functionality.\n\n\n"
