  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Dashboard Elements**\n\nI\'ve successfully finished Requirement 4. I\'m now turning my attention to Requirements 1, 2, and 3. My focus is now on UserDashboard.tsx, starting with the separation of User and Operator Controls. I\'ve begun to consider the `UserDashboardProps`, particularly the `onAcceptBooking` function, to explore how it factors into the separation.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Logic**\n\nI\'m removing functions and elements from `UserDashboard` that simulate operator actions. Specifically, I\'m removing the dispatch simulation button, timer, auto accept feature, and stage advancement. I\'ve also removed the `onAdvanceStage` prop. I am now concentrating on ensuring the user only sees relevant trip info like ETA and driver contact. Next, I\'ll work on locking locations post-booking.\n\n\n**Implementing Booking Restrictions**\n\nI\'m now implementing restrictions around booking, focusing on locking locations during active dispatches. Landmark and hospital popups will no longer offer location setting after the dispatch begins, and will show a relevant message instead. In the `UserDashboard`, I\'ll display pickup and destination as read-only with locked badges. Furthermore, I\'ll disable destination changes from the user panel during active bookings, providing a contact operator message. I\'m also ensuring cancellation is restricted after pickup.\n\n\n**Restricting Cancellation Actions**\n\nI\'m now focusing on restricting the trip cancellation action, ensuring it aligns with specific booking stages. I\'ve implemented logic to determine when cancellation is permissible, and I\'ve removed the button altogether when the trip is beyond that point. When trips are in `transporting`, `at_hospital`, or `completed` stages, a clear banner message with operator contact information is displayed. This change will enforce rules and also prevent the user from mistakenly interacting with the cancellation action.\n\n\n**Reviewing Operator Interactions**\n\nI\'m now revisiting operator interactions, specifically concerning booking cancellations, to align user and operator functionality. I\'m focusing on `UserDashboard.tsx` and the `handleCancelActiveBooking` function to ensure consistency in the user experience. I have reviewed the `App.tsx` and `server.ts` updates, and will now transition to analyzing `OperatorDashboard.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_372930"
