  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Map Component Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the logic within `LeafletMap.tsx`, specifically lines 140-155 regarding setting a destination, and lines 182-205, for setting pickup and drop-off locations. I now understand that when a booking is active (`isLocked = true`), users are prevented from modifying these locations via landmark interactions. This is an important consideration.\n\n\n**Implementing Location Locking**\n\nI\'m now implementing the location locking. I\'ve added the `isLocked` prop to `LeafletMapProps`. When locked, draggable markers are disabled, and popups display messages indicating the locations are locked during dispatch. I\'m updating the pickup and drop-off marker badges to show the locked status with specific messages. Next, I\'ll integrate this into `UserDashboard.tsx` to ensure the confirmed locations are displayed as read-only.\n\n\n**Refining User Messaging**\n\nI\'m now refining the user messaging. Under the \"Hospital Directory\" tab, when `activeBooking` exists and the user views hospitals, I\'ll display a clear message indicating the destination is locked during an active dispatch, and prevent invocation of `onDropoffChange`. I\'ll also add a banner explaining the lock to maintain navigational continuity, and how to request a reroute.\nI\'m also working on Requirement 3, restricting cancellation after pickup, providing clear messaging about in-progress trips.\n\n\n**Enforcing Cancellation Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enforcing the cancellation rules within the booking logic itself, going beyond just hiding the \"Cancel Request\" button. I\'ve examined the `UserDashboard.tsx` component, specifically lines 288-294 concerning the cancel button. The logic hinges on the `isPatientPickedUp` status derived from `activeBooking.stage`. If the patient is picked up (transporting, at hospital, or completed), I\'ll hide the cancel button. I\'ll also add a clear status message in its place.\n\n\n**Preventing In-Progress Cancellation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on restricting cancellations for active trips, going beyond UI restrictions. I\'m leveraging the current booking stage (`transporting`, `at_hospital`, `completed`) to prevent cancellations. I\'m using the provided toast message for the user in `UserDashboard.tsx` and am verifying with the server side logic, in `/api/bookings/:id/stage`. I\'m preventing all non-operator cancellation requests during a trip\'s active phases, returning a 403 error from the server to deny unauthorized requests.\n\n\n"
