  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `OperatorDashboard.tsx` file, specifically lines 293-306. I\'m focusing on how the \"Locations and Symptoms Grid\" is structured using Tailwind CSS classes. I\'m noting the use of a grid layout with responsive adjustments for different screen sizes, specifically the `md:grid-cols-2` which I\'ll be sure to understand. I\'m also examining the styling applied to each grid item.\n\n\n**Adding Rerouting Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating an \"Authorized Operator Reroute/Modify Destination\" feature. My thought is, upon clicking this button, an inline dropdown will appear. It will allow the operator to reroute the ambulance to one of ten verified hospitals. This is useful for diversions or when specialty care is needed. This will be added to the Operator Dashboard.\n\n\n**Implementing Reroute Logic**\n\nI\'m now deep in the rerouting process. I\'m focusing on the `onOperatorReroute` function and how it updates the booking details. This involves updating the drop-off address and coordinates, and the destination hospital ID. I\'m especially interested in the conditional logic that handles trips currently in progress, particularly how the route is recalculated based on the ambulance\'s current state (transporting or en_route_pickup). I\'m also ensuring the toast message confirms the rerouting, and that the UI updates in realtime.\n\n\n**Refactoring Simulation Buttons**\n\nI\'m currently removing simulation buttons from `UserDashboard.tsx` to streamline the user interface. I\'m focusing on lines 255-278, which involve removing various buttons related to dispatch simulations. I\'m also deleting the `autoAcceptSeconds` state and its associated `useEffect` timer, along with the \"Central Dispatch auto-connect\" chip. My main goal is to replace these with customer-facing messages based on trip stage, keeping the UI clean. I\'m removing related props from `UserDashboardProps` as well, as they\'re no longer needed.\n\n\n**Adjusting Stage Messages**\n\nI\'m now implementing new customer-facing messages based on the trip\'s stage. If the stage is `on_scene`, the user will see, \"Priority Transport: Attending to patient at your location.\" For `transporting`, it\'s now, \"Priority Transport: Patient picked up. Ambulance is navigating to emergency ER bay.\" I\'ve adjusted the cancel button logic as well, hiding it completely for in-progress trips, replacing it with a contact message.\n\n\n**Implementing Location Locking**\n\nI\'m now integrating location locking for active trips. I\'m focusing on passing `isLocked={true}` to the `LeafletMap` component when a booking isn\'t completed or cancelled, and updating the active booking details card. I\'ll add locked indicators to both pickup and destination addresses within the card. I\'m ensuring that users can\'t modify the destination hospital from the \"Hospital Directory\" tab when a booking is active, displaying a message or disabling the \"Set as Destination\" button. I\'ll now check `LeafletMap.tsx`.\n\n\n**Adding Map Locking**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `isLocked` prop within the `LeafletMap.tsx` component. I\'m focusing on disabling dragging and changing the cursor on pickup and dropoff markers when `isLocked` is true. Additionally, I am adding a badge to these markers to indicate their locked status. The changes extend to the landmark and hospital markers, and I\'ve ensured that the \"Set as Pickup/Drop-off\" and \"Set as Destination\" buttons are rendered conditionally based on the `isLocked` state, with appropriate messaging when they\'re locked.\n\n\n**Defining Reroute API**\n\nI\'ve just defined the `/api/bookings/:id/reroute` route in `server.ts`. I\'ve implemented the POST endpoint to handle destination rerouting. It updates the booking details with new coordinates, address, destination ID, and route information. I\'ve included validation to ensure the booking exists, and return success/failure messages accordingly.\n\n\n**Validating Cancellation Rules**\n\nI\'m now implementing logic to prevent cancellations for trips in progress. I\'m focusing on the `/api/bookings/:id/stage` route and adding conditional checks. I\'ve implemented a validation to ensure bookings in the \'transporting\', \'at_hospital\', or \'completed\' stages are not cancelled unless requested by an operator. My current focus is to ensure the appropriate error messages are displayed to the user if they try to cancel an active trip. I also need to update this logic in `App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Analyzing Rerouting Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `handleOperatorReroute` function within `App.tsx`. I\'m especially focused on the route recalculation, specifically how the new polyline and estimated time are updated based on the ambulance\'s current location. I\'m ensuring this route update logic functions effectively.\n\n\n**Refining Route Updates**\n\nI\'m now refining the route recalculation after a reroute. I\'ve updated how the new route, including polyline, distance, and ETA, are updated based on the current ambulance position. This is being synchronized with the bookings state. I\'m also ensuring the dropoff state updates are reflected on the map.\n\n\n"
