  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Dashboard Logic**\n\nI\'ve just finished ensuring `LeafletMap.tsx` fully respects the `isLocked` state. Now, I\'m shifting focus to updating `UserDashboard.tsx`. The core change involves removing all operator-only tools, specifically the `onAcceptBooking` function, to streamline the UI.\n\n\n**Streamlining Cancellation Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on restricting booking cancellations based on stage progression. The goal is to prevent cancellations once the patient has been picked up. I\'ve implemented a check against the `activeBooking` stage. If the patient is picked up, in transport, at the hospital, or the booking is completed, the cancellation button will be hidden. Otherwise, the button will be shown. This improves the workflow and prevents unexpected issues.\n\n\n"
