  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\nThe user requested four specific updates to the DropAid emergency ambulance dispatch app without rebuilding the application or breaking working features:\n1. **Separate User and Operator Controls**: Remove all operator-only tools from the User Panel (time skip, auto-accept countdown, simulation stage buttons, manual status controls, reset controls). Keep operator tools exclusively in the Operator Panel or Demo Controls.\n2. **Lock Locations After Booking**: Before booking confirmation, allow location editing. Once submitted, lock both pickup and destination locations in the User Panel (read-only display, disable marker dragging and map popup selection). Allow changes *only* through an authorized operator workflow with route recalculation and synchronization.\n3. **Restrict Cancellation After Pickup**: Allow users to cancel eligible bookings before the driver confirms patient pickup. Once picked up (`transporting`, `at_hospital`, `completed`), disable and hide user cancellation, display: `\"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\"`, and enforce this rule in the booking logic (both frontend and backend).\n4. **Remove Navbar Logo**: Remove the DropAid logo/icon from the navigation bar while preserving the DropAid text branding, alignment, and responsive layout.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed**:\n  - `src/components/Common/Header.tsx`: Removed the siren icon/logo container from navbar while preserving `DropAid` text wordmark, `Emergency Dispatch` badge, alignment, and responsive layout (Req 4).\n  - `server.ts`:\n    - Updated `/api/bookings/:id/stage`: Enforces backend cancellation restriction if booking is in `transporting`, `at_hospital`, or `completed` and request is not authorized by operator (Req 3).\n    - Added `/api/bookings/:id/reroute`: Supports authorized operator rerouting of destination coordinates, address, hospital ID, and updated road polyline (Req 2).\n  - `src/components/Map/LeafletMap.tsx`:\n    - Added `isLocked?: boolean` prop.\n    - Disabled dragging on pickup and dropoff markers when `isLocked` is true.\n    - Updated landmark and hospital marker popups to show read-only locked notices instead of \"Set as Pickup\", \"Set as Drop-off\", or \"Set as Destination\" when `isLocked` is true (Req 2).\n    - Updated marker badges to `\360\237\224\222 CONFIRMED PICKUP` and `\360\237\224\222 CONFIRMED ER BAY`.\n  - `src/components/OperatorDashboard/OperatorDashboard.tsx`:\n    - Added `onOperatorReroute?: (bookingId: string, hospital: Hospital) => void;` prop.\n    - Added `isRerouteOpen` state and interactive authorized operator reroute workflow under \"Route Locations\", allowing the operator to reroute the active trip to any verified hospital in Delhi NCR (Req 2).\n  - `src/components/UserDashboard/UserDashboard.tsx`:\n    - Removed operator simulation props `onAcceptBooking` and `onAdvanceStage` from `UserDashboardProps`.\n    - Removed `autoAcceptSeconds` state and automatic countdown interval.\n    - Removed simulation action buttons (`Accept Dispatch (Simulate Operator)`, `Patient Picked Up (Route to ER)`, `Arrived at Hospital`) (Req 1).\n    - Enforced cancellation rule: hides `Cancel Request` once patient is picked up (`transporting`, `at_hospital`, `completed`) and displays `\"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\"` with `ShieldAlert` icon (Req 3).\n    - Passed `isLocked={true}` to `LeafletMap` during active bookings and disabled onPickupChange/onDropoffChange callbacks (Req 2).\n    - Updated route details card with `\360\237\224\222 Confirmed & Locked` badge (Req 2).\n    - Updated Hospital Directory tab to block destination switching during active bookings with an alert message (Req 2).\n\n- **In Progress / Remaining in `src/App.tsx`**:\n  - Wiring `handleCancelActiveBooking` logic to prevent cancellation once `bk.stage === \'transporting\' || \'at_hospital\' || \'completed\'`.\n  - Adding `handleOperatorReroute` in `App.tsx` to handle the operator reroute workflow, recalculate driving route to the new hospital, update `bookings` & `dropoff` state, and sync via `/api/bookings/:id/reroute`.\n  - Removing `onAcceptBooking` and `onAdvanceStage` props passed to `UserDashboard` in `App.tsx`.\n  - Passing `onOperatorReroute={handleOperatorReroute}` to `OperatorDashboard` in `App.tsx`.\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n- In `App.tsx`: `handleCancelActiveBooking` was simply calling `handleAdvanceStage(bookingId, \'cancelled\')` without checking the current stage. Adding the guard prevents any bypass.\n- In `UserDashboard.tsx`: The component originally received operator functions and had an automatic 6-second timer to auto-accept bookings. Removing this separates user and operator roles cleanly.\n- Operator rerouting needs to handle two scenarios:\n  1. If unit is actively `transporting` (patient in ambulance): immediately recalculates road route from ambulance\'s current location to the new hospital ER using `getDrivingRoute`.\n  2. If unit is `en_route_pickup`, `on_scene`, or `pending`: updates the destination hospital so that when transport begins, the new hospital route is used.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Files modified so far:\n  - `/src/components/Common/Header.tsx` (clean, verified)\n  - `/server.ts` (clean, verified)\n  - `/src/components/Map/LeafletMap.tsx` (clean, verified)\n  - `/src/components/OperatorDashboard/OperatorDashboard.tsx` (clean, verified)\n  - `/src/components/UserDashboard/UserDashboard.tsx` (clean, verified)\n- Only `/src/App.tsx` requires the final replacement chunks.\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. Edit `/src/App.tsx`:\n   - Replace `handleCancelActiveBooking` around line 679 with:\n     ```typescript\n     const handleCancelActiveBooking = (bookingId: string) => {\n       const bk = bookings.find((b) => b.id === bookingId);\n       if (!bk) return;\n       if (\n         bk.stage === \'transporting\' ||\n         bk.stage === \'at_hospital\' ||\n         bk.stage === \'completed\'\n       ) {\n         showToast(\'Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\', \'error\');\n         return;\n       }\n       handleAdvanceStage(bookingId, \'cancelled\');\n     };\n     ```\n   - Add `handleOperatorReroute` function in `App.tsx` right after `handleCancelActiveBooking`:\n     - Updates `booking.dropoffCoords`, `booking.dropoffAddress`, `booking.destinationHospitalId`.\n     - If `bk.stage === \'transporting\'`, recalculates driving route from `assigned.location` to `newDropoffCoords` via `getDrivingRoute`.\n     - Updates `routePolyline`, `routeDistanceKm`, `routeEtaMins`.\n     - Posts to `/api/bookings/${bookingId}/reroute`.\n     - Updates local `dropoff` state and shows toast confirmation.\n   - Update `UserDashboard` JSX render in `App.tsx` (around line 875):\n     - Remove `onAcceptBooking={handleAcceptBooking}` and `onAdvanceStage={handleAdvanceStage}`.\n   - Update `OperatorDashboard` JSX render in `App.tsx` (around line 922):\n     - Add `onOperatorReroute={handleOperatorReroute}`.\n2. Run `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` to verify zero TypeScript/build errors.\n3. Restart dev server (`restart_dev_server`) if necessary.\n4. Provide a clear summary to the user.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Do not rebuild the app or break existing workflows (Leaflet routing, 5-second hold confirmation, 3D telemetry viewer, driver cockpit).\n- The DropAid logo icon in the navbar must remain removed while preserving the text wordmark.\n- Cancellation must be locked programmatically in both frontend and backend after pickup.\n- Locations must be locked in the User Panel once booking is initiated, and editable only via the Operator Panel.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 181
    included_step_index_end: 388
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/bun.lock\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/server.ts\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/components/Booking/HoldToConfirmButton.tsx\n/src/components/Cloudinary/CloudinaryUploadModal.tsx\n/src/components/Common/Header.tsx\n/src/components/Hospitals/HospitalDirectory.tsx\n/src/components/Map/LeafletMap.tsx\n/src/components/OperatorDashboard/OperatorDashboard.tsx\n/src/components/Three/AmbulanceViewer3D.tsx\n/src/components/UserDashboard/UserDashboard.tsx\n/src/data/mockData.ts\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/src/services/audioService.ts\n/src/services/routingService.ts\n/src/types/index.ts\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nleaflet: ^1.9.4\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nthree: ^0.186.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/leaflet: ^1.9.22\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\n@types/three: ^0.186.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls (Interactions API video generation).\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n# CLOUDINARY CONFIGURATION (Optional for production cloud storage):\n# If not provided, DropAid uses high-fidelity local memory / preview fallback.\nCLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=\"demo\"\nCLOUDINARY_API_KEY=\"\"\nCLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=\"\"\nCLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=\"dropaid_uploads\"\n\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>DropAid \342\200\224 Emergency Ambulance Dispatch & Tracking Platform</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Professional emergency ambulance booking platform with live GPS routing, 5-second hold confirmation, interactive Leaflet hospital map, synchronized operator/driver dispatch, 3D telemetry viewer, and AI scene video generation.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"DropAid \342\200\224 Emergency Ambulance Dispatch & Tracking Platform\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Professional emergency ambulance booking platform with live GPS routing, 5-second hold confirmation, interactive Leaflet hospital map, synchronized operator/driver dispatch, 3D telemetry viewer, and AI scene video generation.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n    <link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n    <link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css\" integrity=\"sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=\" crossorigin=\"\" />\n  </head>\n  <body class=\"bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 font-sans antialiased selection:bg-sky-500 selection:text-white\">\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Remix DropAid \342\200\224 by ayushEdit\",\n  \"description\": \"Professional emergency ambulance booking platform with live GPS routing, 5-second hold confirmation, interactive Leaflet hospital map, synchronized operator/driver dispatch, 3D telemetry viewer, and AI scene video generation.\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [\n    \"geolocation\"\n  ],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\n    \"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport React, { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from \'react\';\nimport {\n  ViewMode,\n  Booking,\n  AmbulanceUnit,\n  LatLng,\n  TripStage,\n  PatientProfile,\n  BookingDocument\n} from \'./types/index.ts\';\nimport {\n  HOSPITALS,\n  LANDMARKS,\n  INITIAL_AMBULANCES,\n  INITIAL_PATIENT,\n  INITIAL_DEMO_BOOKING\n} from \'./data/mockData.ts\';\nimport {\n  getDrivingRoute,\n  reverseGeocode,\n  calculateBearing,\n  calculateHaversineDistance,\n  findNearestAvailableAmbulance,\n} from \'./services/routingService.ts\';\nimport { Header } from \'./components/Common/Header.tsx\';\nimport { LeafletMap } from \'./components/Map/LeafletMap.tsx\';\nimport { UserDashboard } from \'./components/UserDashboard/UserDashboard.tsx\';\nimport { OperatorDashboard } from \'./components/OperatorDashboard/OperatorDashboard.tsx\';\nimport { AmbulanceViewer3D } from \'./components/Three/AmbulanceViewer3D.tsx\';\nimport { CloudinaryUploadModal } from \'./components/Cloudinary/CloudinaryUploadModal.tsx\';\nimport { CheckCircle2, AlertCircle, X } from \'lucide-react\';\n\nexport default function App() {\n  // 1. Primary Top Controls State\n  const [currentView, setCurrentView] = useState<ViewMode>(\'user\');\n\n  // 2. Map & Route State (Default: Central Delhi NCR)\n  const [pickup, setPickup] = useState<{ coords: LatLng; address: string }>({\n    coords: { lat: 28.6327, lng: 77.2197 }, // Connaught Place, New Delhi\n    address: \'Connaught Place (Inner Circle), Block A, New Delhi\',\n  });\n\n  const [dropoff, setDropoff] = useState<{ coords: LatLng; address: string; hospitalId?: string }>({\n    coords: { lat: HOSPITALS[0].lat, lng: HOSPITALS[0].lng }, // AIIMS, New Delhi\n    address: `${HOSPITALS[0].name}, ${HOSPITALS[0].address}`,\n    hospitalId: HOSPITALS[0].id,\n  });\n\n  const [routePolyline, setRoutePolyline] = useState<[number, number][]>([]);\n  const [routeDistanceKm, setRouteDistanceKm] = useState<number>(7.8);\n  const [routeEtaMins, setRouteEtaMins] = useState<number>(6);\n  const [routeError, setRouteError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  // 3. Fleet & Bookings Simulation State\n  const [ambulances, setAmbulances] = useState<AmbulanceUnit[]>(() => {\n    const saved = localStorage.getItem(\'dropaid_ambulances\');\n    return saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : INITIAL_AMBULANCES;\n  });\n\n  const [bookings, setBookings] = useState<Booking[]>(() => {\n    const saved = localStorage.getItem(\'dropaid_bookings\');\n    return saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : [INITIAL_DEMO_BOOKING];\n  });\n\n  const [patientProfile, setPatientProfile] = useState<PatientProfile>(INITIAL_PATIENT);\n  const [gpsAccuracy, setGpsAccuracy] = useState<number>(10);\n  const [isDetectingGPS, setIsDetectingGPS] = useState<boolean>(false);\n  const [gpsError, setGpsError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  // 4. Modals State\n  const [is3DViewerOpen, setIs3DViewerOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [isUploadModalOpen, setIsUploadModalOpen] = useState(false);\n  const [uploadCategory, setUploadCategory] = useState<\'id_card\' | \'insurance\' | \'medical_history\' | \'incident_photo\'>(\'insurance\');\n  const [toastMessage, setToastMessage] = useState<{ type: \'success\' | \'info\' | \'error\'; text: string } | null>(null);\n\n  // Active Booking\n  const activeBooking = bookings.find(\n    (b) => b.stage !== \'completed\' && b.stage !== \'cancelled\'\n  ) || null;\n\n  const assignedAmbulance = activeBooking?.assignedUnitId\n    ? ambulances.find((a) => a.id === activeBooking.assignedUnitId) || null\n    : null;\n\n  // Persist State to LocalStorage\n  useEffect(() => {\n    localStorage.setItem(\'dropaid_bookings\', JSON.stringify(bookings));\n  }, [bookings]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    localStorage.setItem(\'dropaid_ambulances\', JSON.stringify(ambulances));\n  }, [ambulances]);\n\n  // Toast Helper\n  const showToast = (text: string, type: \'success\' | \'info\' | \'error\' = \'info\') => {\n    setToastMessage({ text, type });\n    setTimeout(() => setToastMessage(null), 3800);\n  };\n\n  // Recalculate Route whenever pickup or dropoff changes (only when no active trip is running)\n  const calculateCurrentRoute = useCallback(async (start: LatLng, end: LatLng) => {\n    setRouteError(null);\n    try {\n      const result = await getDrivingRoute(start, end);\n      setRoutePolyline(result.polyline);\n      setRouteDistanceKm(result.distanceKm);\n      setRouteEtaMins(result.etaMinutes);\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      console.warn(\'Failed to calculate route:\', err);\n      setRouteError(\'Route service calculating road grid path.\');\n    }\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // If there is no active booking in progress, show planned pickup -> dropoff route preview\n    if (!activeBooking) {\n      calculateCurrentRoute(pickup.coords, dropoff.coords);\n    }\n  }, [pickup.coords, dropoff.coords, activeBooking, calculateCurrentRoute]);\n\n  // GPS Location Detection with Graceful Error & Permission Handling\n  const handleDetectGPS = useCallback(() => {\n    if (!navigator.geolocation) {\n      const msg = \'Geolocation is not supported by your browser.\';\n      setGpsError(msg);\n      showToast(msg, \'error\');\n      return;\n    }\n\n    setIsDetectingGPS(true);\n    setGpsError(null);\n\n    navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(\n      async (pos) => {\n        const coords = { lat: pos.coords.latitude, lng: pos.coords.longitude };\n        const accuracy = Math.round(pos.coords.accuracy || 12);\n        setGpsAccuracy(accuracy);\n        setGpsError(null);\n\n        const address = await reverseGeocode(coords.lat, coords.lng);\n        setPickup({ coords, address });\n        setIsDetectingGPS(false);\n        showToast(`GPS Position detected: ${address.split(\',\')[0]} (\302\261${accuracy}m)`, \'success\');\n      },\n      (err) => {\n        setIsDetectingGPS(false);\n        let errorMsg = \'GPS location unavailable.\';\n        if (err.code === err.PERMISSION_DENIED) {\n          errorMsg = \'Location permission was denied by browser. Please enable location permissions or select your address below.\';\n        } else if (err.code === err.POSITION_UNAVAILABLE) {\n          errorMsg = \'GPS satellite fix or network position is currently unavailable.\';\n        } else if (err.code === err.TIMEOUT) {\n          errorMsg = \'GPS location request timed out.\';\n        }\n        setGpsError(errorMsg);\n        showToast(errorMsg, \'error\');\n      },\n      { enableHighAccuracy: true, timeout: 7000, maximumAge: 10000 }\n    );\n  }, []);\n\n  // Map Change Handlers\n  const handlePickupChange = (coords: LatLng, address: string) => {\n    setPickup({ coords, address });\n  };\n\n  const handleDropoffChange = (coords: LatLng, address: string, hospitalId?: string) => {\n    setDropoff({ coords, address, hospitalId });\n  };\n\n  // CREATE EMERGENCY BOOKING (Nearest Ambulance Dispatch from Hospital or Highway Patrol)\n  const handleCreateBooking = async (\n    equipmentIds: string[],\n    notes: string,\n    bookingType: \'emergency_hold\' | \'manual\' = \'emergency_hold\'\n  ) => {\n    // 1. Calculate nearest available ambulance across Delhi NCR\n    const nearestResult = findNearestAvailableAmbulance(pickup.coords, ambulances);\n    const assigned = nearestResult\n      ? nearestResult.ambulance\n      : ambulances.find((a) => a.status === \'available\') || ambulances[0];\n\n    // 2. Fetch Phase 1 road route: from assigned ambulance\'s current location to patient pickup\n    let phase1Polyline: [number, number][] = [];\n    let dispatchDistKm = nearestResult?.distanceKm || 4.2;\n    let dispatchEtaMins = nearestResult?.etaMinutes || 5;\n\n    try {\n      const leg1 = await getDrivingRoute(assigned.location, pickup.coords);\n      phase1Polyline = leg1.polyline;\n      dispatchDistKm = leg1.distanceKm;\n      dispatchEtaMins = leg1.etaMinutes;\n    } catch {\n      phase1Polyline = [\n        [assigned.location.lat, assigned.location.lng],\n        [pickup.coords.lat, pickup.coords.lng],\n      ];\n    }\n\n    setRoutePolyline(phase1Polyline);\n... (truncated)\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n@layer base {\n  body {\n    font-family: \'Plus Jakarta Sans\', system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;\n  }\n  \n  code, pre, .font-mono {\n    font-family: \'JetBrains Mono\', monospace;\n    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;\n  }\n}\n\n/* Leaflet map fixups */\n.leaflet-container {\n  font-family: inherit;\n  z-index: 10;\n  width: 100%;\n  height: 100%;\n}\n\n.leaflet-popup-content-wrapper {\n  border-radius: 0.75rem;\n  padding: 0.25rem;\n  box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 8px 10px -6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n}\n\n.leaflet-popup-content {\n  margin: 0.75rem 1rem;\n  font-size: 0.875rem;\n  line-height: 1.25rem;\n}\n\n/* Custom pulsed radar ring for emergency vehicles */\n@keyframes siren-pulse {\n  0% { transform: scale(0.9); opacity: 0.9; }\n  50% { transform: scale(1.4); opacity: 0.3; }\n  100% { transform: scale(1.8); opacity: 0; }\n}\n\n.siren-ring {\n  animation: siren-pulse 1.8s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1) infinite;\n}\n\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "Modify the existing DropAid application without rebuilding it.\n\n1. **Remove the Map from Home:** Completely remove the map currently displayed on the homepage. Keep the homepage clean, professional, and focused on ambulance booking.\n\n2. **Show Map After Booking Initiation:** Display the interactive map only after the user successfully holds the red booking button for 5 seconds or submits a manual booking form. Open the map in the booking/tracking interface immediately after submission.\n\n3. **Accurate Location:** Center the map on the user\'s actual GPS pickup location, with permission, or their manually selected pickup point. Display the pickup marker, destination marker, assigned ambulance, and road-following route when available.\n\n4. **Dynamic Tracking:** Initially show the pickup location and ambulance-search status. Display the assigned ambulance and its route after operator acceptance. Update the route and vehicle position as the trip progresses.\n\n**Quality Control:** Ensure both booking methods open the same map interface, preserve booking details, prevent duplicate requests, and handle GPS permission or routing failures gracefully. Verify the map never appears on the homepage and remains accessible throughout the active trip. Preserve existing styling, responsiveness, and working features."
    user_requests: "Fix the ambulance route transition bug in the existing DropAid application without rebuilding the app or changing its design.\n\n**Problem:** After the ambulance picks up the patient, the map continues displaying the old route to the pickup location instead of showing the route to the hospital destination.\n\n**Required Fix:**\n1. When the trip status changes to **\342\200\234Patient Picked Up\342\200\235**, immediately remove the previous pickup route and request a new road-following route from the ambulance\342\200\231s current position to the selected hospital.\n2. Update the destination marker, route polyline, ETA, distance, and navigation instructions.\n3. Animate the ambulance along the new route\342\200\231s actual road coordinates. Never reuse stale route coordinates or draw a straight-line path.\n4. Synchronize the updated route across User and Operator views.\n5. Prevent race conditions by ignoring outdated routing responses and clearing obsolete route layers before rendering the new route.\n6. If routing fails, display a clear error and retry option instead of retaining the misleading old route.\n\n**Quality Control:** Test the complete flow: booking \342\206\222 driver acceptance \342\206\222 ambulance en route to pickup \342\206\222 patient picked up \342\206\222 new hospital route displayed \342\206\222 hospital arrival. Verify that the old route disappears immediately, the new route begins at the ambulance\342\200\231s current position, and all map markers, ETA, and trip statuses remain synchronized. Preserve all existing working features."
    user_requests: "Update the existing DropAid application. Fix the following issues without rebuilding the app or breaking working features.\n\n**1. Separate User and Operator Controls**\n- Remove all operator-only tools from the User Panel, including time skip, trip-stage simulation buttons, manual status controls, and reset controls.\n- Keep these tools exclusively in the Operator Panel or Demo Controls.\n- Ensure users can only access customer-facing booking and tracking features.\n\n**2. Lock Locations After Booking**\n- Before booking confirmation, allow users to edit pickup and destination locations.\n- Once a booking is submitted, lock both locations and prevent changes from the User Panel.\n- Display the confirmed pickup and destination as read-only.\n- Allow location changes only through an authorized operator workflow, with route recalculation and synchronized updates.\n\n**3. Restrict Cancellation After Pickup**\n- Allow users to cancel an eligible booking before the driver confirms patient pickup.\n- Once the patient is picked up, disable user cancellation and hide or remove the cancellation action.\n- Display a clear message: \"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\"\n- Enforce these rules in the booking logic, not just by hiding the button.\n\n**4. Remove Navbar Logo**\n- Remove the DropAid logo/icon from the navigation bar while preserving the DropAid text branding, alignment, and responsive layout.\n\n**Quality Control:** Test user and operator permissions, location locking, cancellation before and after pickup, route synchronization, and mobile responsiveness. Prevent unauthorized state changes, stale data, and duplicate actions. Fix all console errors and verify existing booking and tracking workflows still function correctly."
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
  }
}
