  planner_response {
    response: "The requested updates have been implemented and verified:\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Separated User and Operator Controls**\n   - Removed all operator simulation controls from the User Panel (time skip, auto-accept countdown, stage simulation buttons, and manual status controls).\n   - The User Panel is now strictly customer-facing for booking, GPS detection, and real-time trip tracking.\n   - All dispatch simulation, stage progression, unit reassignment, and trip management tools remain exclusively inside the Operator Panel.\n\n2. **Locked Locations After Booking**\n   - Before booking confirmation, users can freely adjust pickup coordinates, GPS detect, search landmarks, and select destination hospitals.\n   - Upon booking submission, pickup and dropoff locations are locked in the User Panel with read-only badges and disabled map pin dragging (`isLocked={true}`). Landmark and hospital map popups now show read-only confirmed notices instead of selection buttons.\n   - Authorized location rerouting is available exclusively through the Operator Dashboard (\"Reroute Destination\"), which recalculates road routes, updates ETA and distances, and syncs across views and the backend.\n\n3. **Restricted Cancellation After Patient Pickup**\n   - Users can cancel their booking while the ambulance is en route to pickup or on scene.\n   - Once the patient has been picked up (`transporting`, `at_hospital`, `completed`), user cancellation is disabled and hidden, displaying:\n     > *\"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\"*\n   - Enforced programmatically in both frontend handlers and backend API endpoint validation.\n\n4. **Removed Navbar Logo**\n   - Removed the siren icon/logo container from the header navigation bar while preserving the `DropAid` wordmark branding, \"Emergency Dispatch\" badge, alignment, and responsive design."
    modified_response: "The requested updates have been implemented and verified:\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Separated User and Operator Controls**\n   - Removed all operator simulation controls from the User Panel (time skip, auto-accept countdown, stage simulation buttons, and manual status controls).\n   - The User Panel is now strictly customer-facing for booking, GPS detection, and real-time trip tracking.\n   - All dispatch simulation, stage progression, unit reassignment, and trip management tools remain exclusively inside the Operator Panel.\n\n2. **Locked Locations After Booking**\n   - Before booking confirmation, users can freely adjust pickup coordinates, GPS detect, search landmarks, and select destination hospitals.\n   - Upon booking submission, pickup and dropoff locations are locked in the User Panel with read-only badges and disabled map pin dragging (`isLocked={true}`). Landmark and hospital map popups now show read-only confirmed notices instead of selection buttons.\n   - Authorized location rerouting is available exclusively through the Operator Dashboard (\"Reroute Destination\"), which recalculates road routes, updates ETA and distances, and syncs across views and the backend.\n\n3. **Restricted Cancellation After Patient Pickup**\n   - Users can cancel their booking while the ambulance is en route to pickup or on scene.\n   - Once the patient has been picked up (`transporting`, `at_hospital`, `completed`), user cancellation is disabled and hidden, displaying:\n     > *\"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\"*\n   - Enforced programmatically in both frontend handlers and backend API endpoint validation.\n\n4. **Removed Navbar Logo**\n   - Removed the siren icon/logo container from the header navigation bar while preserving the `DropAid` wordmark branding, \"Emergency Dispatch\" badge, alignment, and responsive design."
