  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Interface Requirements**\n\nI\'m now meticulously dissecting Requirement 1. My focus is on the crucial separation of operator and user interfaces. I\'m imagining the operator\'s dashboard with its fleet map, request influx, active trips, driver stats, and trip records. Simultaneously, I am making the changes, that were previously required by the user interface.\n\n\n**Refining Dispatch Logic**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the auto-dispatch feature. My focus is now on streamlining the workflow; I\'m eliminating the manual \"Accept Dispatch\" step, which is a key update. Now, the system automatically assigns ambulances based on proximity and availability. Operators retain the power to override, so their role remains pivotal. I will be updating how the booking\'s `stage` attribute changes.\n\n\n**Automating Unit Assignment**\n\nMy current focus is on automating the ambulance assignment process. The system now immediately finds the nearest available unit, assigns it, calculates a road route, and dispatches the unit. I\'ve integrated a route calculation component to handle dynamic rerouting and updates. If a unit isn\'t immediately available, it remains pending for auto-dispatch. Operators will still be able to override assignments and reroute, using a modal/dropdown.\n\n\n"
