  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Cloudinary Integration**\n\nI\'m now diving into Requirement 4, specifically the Cloudinary integration. The key focus is on confirming end-to-end functionality. I need to verify image uploads, previews, and optimized delivery. Furthermore, the plan is to replace existing hospital, driver, and ambulance images with Cloudinary versions. Security is a priority, so I\'ll be working with secure backend-signed uploads, or a restricted unsigned upload preset. API secrets will be kept server-side, of course.\n\n\n**Implementing Database Persistence**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating Cloudinary asset information with the database. Specifically, I\'m storing the returned URLs and public IDs after each upload. Error handling is crucial; I\'m building safeguards for failed uploads, ensuring proper response to invalid file types, missing configuration, and safe handling of deletions and replacements. I\'ll thoroughly test real uploads and retrieval to ensure functionality. I\'ve begun reviewing the database structure to determine image replacement and update implementation for `Hospital` and `AmbulanceUnit`.\n\n\n"
