  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Hospital Data Updates**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `HospitalDirectory.tsx`. I\'ve outlined two key approaches: either accept an `onUpdateHospitalImage` callback, or directly handle the `hospitals` prop. The goal is to ensure hospital photo updates trigger state changes and persist. Now I\'m evaluating the pros and cons of these options, and the integration of a UI element for photo upload/replacement.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Uploads**\n\nI\'m now delving into the backend, specifically `server.ts`. I\'m going to maintain a mutable copy of `HOSPITALS` to ensure persistence across API calls. I\'m implementing the `/api/hospitals/:id/image` endpoint to handle image updates and Cloudinary integration, alongside similar updates for fleet entities. Furthermore, I\'m integrating auto-dispatch in `/api/bookings` for new bookings, immediately assigning available ambulances and updating their status. I\'m also planning a background daily ride simulation.\n\n\n**Developing Simulation Features**\n\nI\'m now focused on building the simulation engine within `server.ts` to generate realistic emergency rides. I\'m implementing API endpoints for control and state retrieval. I\'m aiming for about 20 simulated rides, each with realistic data like patient info, location, timestamps, and ambulance assignments. These rides will advance through various lifecycle stages, freeing up ambulances upon completion.\n\n\n**Managing Simulation Timers**\n\nI\'ve just added robust timer management to the simulation. The server now has a single `simulationTimer` interval. Pauses or resets call `clearInterval` to avoid duplicates or race conditions on navigation or refresh.\n\n\\n\\n\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the Cloudinary integration. I\'m validating the input file types accepted and restricting file sizes. I am making real signed uploads or handling unsigned uploads, depending on Cloudinary configuration, and returning the structured response. Unsupported files and Cloudinary credential issues will get proper 400 errors.\n\n\n"
