  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Mapping Data and Plan**\n\nI\'ve got the mock data \342\200\223 rich with hospitals, landmarks, and ambulances spread across Delhi, Noida, and Haryana. My focus is structuring a plan to meet the 4 requirements. Right now, I\'m thinking of creating a `server.ts` with a `serverHospitals` in-memory mutable copy initialized with `HOSPITALS`.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Structures**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating `serverAmbulances`, an in-memory mutable copy initialized with `INITIAL_AMBULANCES`, alongside `serverBookings` to store all booking data. I\'ve begun outlining the API endpoints: `GET /api/hospitals`, `POST /api/hospitals/:id/image`, and similar ones for ambulances. I\'m focusing on auto-dispatch logic: if the ambulance is free, I will assign the nearest available unit automatically. I also intend to handle rerouting and manual overrides.\n\n\n**Developing Simulation Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now building out the simulation engine to generate realistic rides, tracking `simulationState`, and adding endpoints like `/api/simulation` and control methods for start, pause, and reset. The engine will update the simulated time and create rides. Every tick, it\'ll generate bookings, manage ambulance status, and update the simulation state. The objective is to make all rides realistic, so I\'m focusing on the distribution.\n\n\n**Designing Operator Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the operator dashboard design. I\'m prioritizing a dedicated navigation bar with views for \"Fleet Overview & Live Map,\" \"Active Dispatches\" with live stage monitors, and \"Incoming Queue\" with auto-dispatch status. I\'m also including \"Ambulance & Driver Availability\" and a \"Trip History\" section. Finally, there\'s a \"Daily Simulation Engine\" view with controls and progress monitoring.\n\n\n**Refining Dashboard Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating a map component into the operator dashboard, displaying all 14 ambulances across Delhi NCR, including active trip polylines and hospital locations. I\'m focusing on an auto-dispatch monitor that clearly indicates the active proximity algorithms. Override controls will be available, and all simulated rides will have clear `[SIMULATED DATA]` badges. Additionally, I\'ve completely removed the \"Verified Hospital Directory\" section from the user dashboard for a streamlined experience.\n\n\n"
