  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Server State**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the `server.ts` file. I\'ve initialized key server components, including `serverHospitals`, `serverAmbulances`, and `serverBookings` with appropriate data. The next major step involves building the automated daily ride simulation. I\'m starting to think about what the simulation state will entail.\n\n\n**Defining Simulation Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core of the simulation. I\'ve defined the `simulationState` structure, establishing its initial properties. My focus is now on developing the key functions to advance the simulated clock, generate rides, and manage ambulance assignments, and also developing several routes related to the simulation. I\'m aiming for realistic ride simulation and ambulance availability. I also have an interval timer in mind to make the simulation maintain a clean single interval. I am also planning Cloudinary endpoints.\n\n\n**Implementing Cloudinary Integration**\n\nI\'ve just finished outlining the Cloudinary API endpoints. I\'ve designed routes for file uploads, deletions, and updates, ensuring robust error handling. I\'m focusing on file type and size validation and secure uploads using signed credentials or upload presets. Also, endpoints for updating hospital images, fleet photos, and overriding ambulance assignments in bookings are in development. I\'m also planning the auto-dispatch feature in the bookings endpoint.\n\n\n"
