  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Proximity Assignments**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! When a user schedules a booking, `server.ts` now automatically matches them with the closest available ambulance using location proximity. I also figured out how to replicate this proximity assignment on the client, or use the `/api/bookings` response. I\'m exploring the implications for immediate dispatch.\n\n\n**Refining Route Assignments**\n\nI\'m now refining the route assignments. I\'ve integrated a system where, after identifying the nearest ambulance, I calculate the driving route using `getDrivingRoute`. This provides accurate polyline data, distance, and ETA. In cases where route calculation fails, I\'ve implemented a fallback mechanism, ensuring the initial assignment still proceeds using a straight line approximation. I\'m updating the ambulance\'s status to \'en_route_pickup\' and reflecting this change in the ambulance data.\n\n\n**Implementing Instant Dispatch**\n\nI\'ve streamlined the dispatch process. When an ambulance is assigned, I\'m now providing immediate feedback to the user via a toast message, displaying the assigned unit\'s call sign. If no unit is available, I present a message indicating the ongoing search. I\'m also ensuring the booking is initialized with an `initialStage`, `assignedUnitId`, and `routePolyline`. This enhances the user experience by providing instant, relevant updates.\n\n\n**Synchronizing Application Data**\n\nI\'ve implemented a robust data synchronization strategy. I\'m now fetching and merging data for bookings, ambulances, and hospitals from the server every three seconds, ensuring the local state mirrors the latest server updates. I\'ve also incorporated error handling to prevent disruptions in case of network issues, keeping the data sync quiet in the background. My focus now is on testing and optimizing this continuous synchronization process.\n\n\n**Managing Simulation Control**\n\nI\'ve integrated simulation control features. I can now pause and resume the daily ride simulation, reflected in the `simulationState`. I\'ve also implemented the ability to adjust the simulation speed. I\'m focusing on ensuring these features integrate seamlessly with existing functionalities, providing comprehensive control over the simulation environment.\n\n\n**Defining Asset Upload Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently working on defining asset upload functionality. I\'ve established a `useState` hook for `uploadCategory` and created functions to manage opening modals for different asset types, like hospital and driver photos. My logic now includes state updates and server persist operations when assets are uploaded. I\'m focusing on ensuring these updates are handled seamlessly and efficiently.\n\n\n**Implementing Asset Persistency**\n\nI\'ve completed the asset persistency. For hospital photos, I\'m updating the image URL and public ID on the server and state. Driver photos have similar logic. I\'m persisting the new driver photo URL and public ID to the fleet API. This covers the full lifecycle, including error handling and success toasts.\n\n\n"
