  planner_response {
    response: "The DropAid application has been upgraded with dedicated operator architecture, automated ride simulation, streamlined hospital navigation, and complete Cloudinary asset management:\n\n### 1. Separated Operator and User Interfaces\n- **Dedicated Operator Dashboard**: Equipped with a full-viewport **Delhi NCR Fleet Map**, incoming emergency request queue, active trips controller with stage advancement, driver and fleet availability telemetry (fuel %, battery %, rating, base bay), and comprehensive trip history.\n- **Removed User-Style Location Dragging**: The operator map locks coordinates and disables customer-style pin dragging (`isLocked={true}`) to preserve dispatch continuity.\n- **Autonomous Proximity Dispatch**: Requests are automatically evaluated using Haversine distance and real-time road driving routes to dispatch the nearest available ambulance immediately (`en_route_pickup`). Operators monitor active dispatches and can override assignments anytime via the **\"Override Assignment\"** control.\n- **Strict Role Boundaries**: Patient-facing booking and tracking features are cleanly separated from operator tools.\n\n### 2. Automated Daily Ride Simulation\n- **Realistic 24-Hour Simulation Engine**: Runs on a background interval generating ~20 realistic emergency rides per simulated day across Delhi NCR, distributed randomly across simulated hours and minutes.\n- **Full Trip Lifecycle**: Simulates 911 calls, nearest ambulance auto-dispatch, patient pickup, transit to destination hospital ER, and unit release back to base bays upon completion.\n- **Telemetry & Persistent Audit Trail**: Each simulated ride stores a unique ID (`SIM-####`), timestamps, full status history (`pending` \342\206\222 `en_route_pickup` \342\206\222 `on_scene` \342\206\222 `transporting` \342\206\222 `at_hospital` \342\206\222 `completed`), driver, and hospital in persistent storage.\n- **Operator Simulation Controls**: Interactive `Start / Resume`, `Pause`, `Reset`, and speed multiplier (`1x`, `5x`, `10x`, `30x`) controls with timer deduplication safeguards.\n- **Transparent Labeling**: Simulated rides are marked with violet `[SIMULATED DATA]` badges, distinct tracking codes, and honest in-app disclaimers explaining that simulation runs during active sessions.\n\n### 3. Streamlined Hospital Directory\n- **Clean Homepage**: Removed the entire \"Verified Hospital Directory\" section below the red booking button, keeping the patient home screen fast, clean, and 100% focused on emergency booking.\n- **Exclusive Navbar Access**: Hospital listings are now accessible exclusively through the **Hospitals** category in the top navigation bar, featuring region filtering (Delhi, Noida, Haryana), live ICU bed telemetry, ER wait times, direct emergency calling, and destination selection.\n\n### 4. Cloudinary Integration\n- **Server-Side Security**: Secure backend-signed uploads with SHA-1 signatures and restricted upload preset fallback. API secrets remain strictly server-side.\n- **End-to-End Asset Replacement**: Added direct Cloudinary upload and replacement for:\n  - Hospital emergency facility photos (`POST /api/hospitals/:id/image`)\n  - Paramedic driver photos & ambulance units (`POST /api/fleet/:id/photo`)\n  - Patient insurance and medical document attachments (`POST /api/cloudinary/upload`)\n- **Validation & Safe Handling**: Enforced file format verification (JPEG, PNG, WEBP, PDF), 20MB file size limits, optimized CDN delivery badges (`Cloudinary CDN`), and asset deletion/replacement handling."
    modified_response: "The DropAid application has been upgraded with dedicated operator architecture, automated ride simulation, streamlined hospital navigation, and complete Cloudinary asset management:\n\n### 1. Separated Operator and User Interfaces\n- **Dedicated Operator Dashboard**: Equipped with a full-viewport **Delhi NCR Fleet Map**, incoming emergency request queue, active trips controller with stage advancement, driver and fleet availability telemetry (fuel %, battery %, rating, base bay), and comprehensive trip history.\n- **Removed User-Style Location Dragging**: The operator map locks coordinates and disables customer-style pin dragging (`isLocked={true}`) to preserve dispatch continuity.\n- **Autonomous Proximity Dispatch**: Requests are automatically evaluated using Haversine distance and real-time road driving routes to dispatch the nearest available ambulance immediately (`en_route_pickup`). Operators monitor active dispatches and can override assignments anytime via the **\"Override Assignment\"** control.\n- **Strict Role Boundaries**: Patient-facing booking and tracking features are cleanly separated from operator tools.\n\n### 2. Automated Daily Ride Simulation\n- **Realistic 24-Hour Simulation Engine**: Runs on a background interval generating ~20 realistic emergency rides per simulated day across Delhi NCR, distributed randomly across simulated hours and minutes.\n- **Full Trip Lifecycle**: Simulates 911 calls, nearest ambulance auto-dispatch, patient pickup, transit to destination hospital ER, and unit release back to base bays upon completion.\n- **Telemetry & Persistent Audit Trail**: Each simulated ride stores a unique ID (`SIM-####`), timestamps, full status history (`pending` \342\206\222 `en_route_pickup` \342\206\222 `on_scene` \342\206\222 `transporting` \342\206\222 `at_hospital` \342\206\222 `completed`), driver, and hospital in persistent storage.\n- **Operator Simulation Controls**: Interactive `Start / Resume`, `Pause`, `Reset`, and speed multiplier (`1x`, `5x`, `10x`, `30x`) controls with timer deduplication safeguards.\n- **Transparent Labeling**: Simulated rides are marked with violet `[SIMULATED DATA]` badges, distinct tracking codes, and honest in-app disclaimers explaining that simulation runs during active sessions.\n\n### 3. Streamlined Hospital Directory\n- **Clean Homepage**: Removed the entire \"Verified Hospital Directory\" section below the red booking button, keeping the patient home screen fast, clean, and 100% focused on emergency booking.\n- **Exclusive Navbar Access**: Hospital listings are now accessible exclusively through the **Hospitals** category in the top navigation bar, featuring region filtering (Delhi, Noida, Haryana), live ICU bed telemetry, ER wait times, direct emergency calling, and destination selection.\n\n### 4. Cloudinary Integration\n- **Server-Side Security**: Secure backend-signed uploads with SHA-1 signatures and restricted upload preset fallback. API secrets remain strictly server-side.\n- **End-to-End Asset Replacement**: Added direct Cloudinary upload and replacement for:\n  - Hospital emergency facility photos (`POST /api/hospitals/:id/image`)\n  - Paramedic driver photos & ambulance units (`POST /api/fleet/:id/photo`)\n  - Patient insurance and medical document attachments (`POST /api/cloudinary/upload`)\n- **Validation & Safe Handling**: Enforced file format verification (JPEG, PNG, WEBP, PDF), 20MB file size limits, optimized CDN delivery badges (`Cloudinary CDN`), and asset deletion/replacement handling."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\215\002\n\212\002\001i\024}\023\000\206K\364\3310\035F\276\023\016\203^\366\366o\2366t\2533\232Y\342\231\203d\244\312\204\306\211*\225#\027\352h\246\"\b\301\211\346\327\241\261\320J\240\311\036h\201\223\001(\365\274<\252\231\240\350\327:<\031\t\231)v.a6\326\344i\306\253\346\a\333\344\\z\211:\243i\365\t\225\375\321\341\351?\302\311b\365\314S\214\370\320\245x\247\301\233\333\234\"\033\354s\355\264\031\261\214M]\315`\334\372!\020m\371\276Tv\226\240\204\272\236\270\210\315\343#J9\202/\205)\037LT\236K\367<\310ewy\220\200x\n\0202\350j4\264|:;\235:\375s.\341\253\222\032\314;\373\317\305646\344t\003y\a\032|}\217\216\274(\330\361\271\266\022fY9\361\364I\343Rf\267\251\322\341fj\023\bq\226\352\260\026\300rT\264E\273f\345o<\266W\361\314\335|\324\372\250\031MA$\320\a\031h\273\236"
