  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\nUpgrade the existing DropAid application according to 4 explicit requirements:\n1. **User Profile Management**: View, edit, save personal profile (name, phone, email, profile photo, emergency contact name/relationship/phone, blood type, allergies, medical conditions, insurance). Add dedicated \"My Profile\" page accessible from user navigation menu. Persist in database (`GET /api/profile`, `POST /api/profile` + localStorage). Integrate Cloudinary for profile photo uploads with validation.\n2. **Remove Simulation Card**: Completely remove the \"Automated Daily Ride Simulation\" card from `OperatorDashboard.tsx`, including schedule, progress counters, speed controls, Pause, and Reset buttons. Preserve fleet map, incoming requests, active trips, driver availability, trip history, and admin tools.\n3. **Fix Actual Ambulance Movement**:\n   - Animate the vehicle marker continuously along road-route coordinates returned by routing service.\n   - Realistic speed, updating marker position, heading, remaining distance, ETA, and trip status.\n   - Keep movement synchronized across User and Operator dashboards.\n   - Prevent stale routes, frozen markers, duplicate timers, and movement restarting after component re-renders.\n   - After pickup (`en_route_pickup` \342\206\222 `on_scene` \342\206\222 `transporting`), recalculate route from ambulance\'s current position to destination hospital.\n   - Stop movement on complete or cancel.\n4. **Automatic Dispatch**: Remove operator requirement to manually start a simulation. Keep app ready to receive bookings automatically. Match nearest available ambulance and assign driver within **5 seconds** (visual search / countdown, immediate update). If no ambulance is available, display clear status and retry option instead of false confirmation.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Initial Setup Inspected**:\n  - `src/components/Map/LeafletMap.tsx`: Analyzed lines 1-140. Leaflet map renders hospitals, pickup/dropoff, and ambulances.\n  - Previous work already implemented base routing (`getDrivingRoute`), 10 verified hospitals, and 14 ambulances across Delhi, Noida, Haryana.\n  - `server.ts` has Cloudinary proxy (`/api/cloudinary/upload`), booking endpoints, fleet endpoints, and hospital endpoints.\n- **Incomplete / Pending Work**:\n  - `server.ts`: Add `GET /api/profile` and `POST /api/profile` endpoints.\n  - `src/types/index.ts`: Add `email`, `profilePhoto`, `profilePhotoPublicId` to `PatientProfile`. Add profile view mode or modal state.\n  - `src/components/Profile/UserProfileModal.tsx` or `UserProfileView.tsx`: Build the dedicated \"My Profile\" view/modal with Cloudinary photo upload.\n  - `src/components/Common/Header.tsx`: Add \"My Profile\" navigation link/button.\n  - `src/components/OperatorDashboard/OperatorDashboard.tsx`: Strip out the entire Automated Daily Ride Simulation header banner and controls, retaining all other operational features (fleet map, incoming requests, active trips with override, driver availability with Cloudinary photo update, trip history).\n  - `src/components/Map/LeafletMap.tsx` and `src/App.tsx`: Refactor vehicle animation logic so that when a booking is active (`en_route_pickup` or `transporting`), the vehicle moves step-by-step along `routePolyline` with a dedicated, single interval/rAF ref, updating heading (`calculateBearing`), ETA, distance, and synchronizing position across both User and Operator dashboards via `booking.currentVehiclePosition` or server sync.\n  - `src/App.tsx`: Auto-dispatch countdown / matching within 5 seconds for user emergency bookings, with explicit \"No units available\" warning and retry button when all 14 units are busy.\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Technical Constraints\n- `LeafletMap.tsx` currently relies on static marker positions or unmanaged waypoint indices that reset on re-render.\n- Movement must be stored or synchronized in the active `booking.currentVehiclePosition` and `ambulance.location` so both UserDashboard and OperatorDashboard maps reflect the exact same position.\n- In `server.ts`, when a booking transitions to `transporting`, a new driving route is fetched from the ambulance position to `dropoffCoords`, and `routePolyline` is updated.\n- Cloudinary uploads for profile photos need category `profile_photo`, image format validation, and persistence of `photoUrl` and `publicId` in `patientProfile`.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Workspace root: `/` (file paths start with `/`, shell in `/app/applet`).\n- Dev server runs on port 3000 using `tsx server.ts` with Vite middleware.\n- Cloudinary credentials configured in environment with signed proxy in `server.ts`.\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **Types (`/src/types/index.ts`)**:\n   - Update `PatientProfile` to include `email: string; profilePhoto: string; profilePhotoPublicId?: string;`.\n   - Update `ViewMode` if needed or add `\'profile\'` view mode (`\'user\' | \'operator\' | \'hospitals\' | \'profile\'`).\n2. **Server (`/server.ts`)**:\n   - Add persistent `serverProfile` initialized with `INITIAL_PATIENT`.\n   - Add `GET /api/profile` and `POST /api/profile`.\n   - Clean up simulation timer/endpoints if necessary or keep passive, but remove the simulation card from the Operator UI.\n3. **Operator Dashboard (`/src/components/OperatorDashboard/OperatorDashboard.tsx`)**:\n   - Delete the entire top \"SIMULATION STATUS & ENGINE HEADER BANNER\" (lines 95-207) and any simulation tabs/buttons.\n   - Keep Fleet Map, Active Trips, Incoming Queue, Driver & Fleet Availability, and Trip History.\n4. **User Profile View (`/src/components/Profile/UserProfileView.tsx`)**:\n   - Create comprehensive profile page: Name, Phone, Email, Profile Photo (with Cloudinary upload + preview), Blood Type, Allergies, Medical Conditions, Insurance Provider, Policy Number, Emergency Contact (Name, Relationship, Phone).\n   - \"Save Changes\" button calling `POST /api/profile` and updating localStorage.\n5. **Navbar Navigation (`/src/components/Common/Header.tsx`)**:\n   - Add \"My Profile\" button in the header nav (next to Hospitals and 3D Fleet Inspector), switching `currentView` to `\'profile\'`.\n6. **Ambulance Movement Engine (`/src/components/Map/LeafletMap.tsx` & `/src/App.tsx`)**:\n   - Implement continuous interpolation along `routePolyline` with single timer/rAF.\n   - Update assigned ambulance marker position and orientation (`transform: rotate(...)`).\n   - Sync remaining distance and ETA smoothly.\n   - Handle phase transition: when ambulance reaches pickup point (`distance < 30m` or end of polyline), trigger arrival at scene (`on_scene`), then advance to `transporting` with recalculated route to hospital ER, and stop at hospital (`at_hospital` / `completed`).\n7. **5-Second Automatic Dispatch (`/src/App.tsx`)**:\n   - When user clicks emergency hold / manual dispatch, show 5-second radar searching animation (\"Matching nearest available emergency unit...\").\n   - Within 5 seconds: evaluate available units; if available, assign nearest unit, compute route, dispatch; if no units are available, show clear warning with \"Retry Search\" button.\n8. **Compile & Lint Verification**:\n   - Run `lint_applet` and `compile_applet`.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Do NOT rebuild the application from scratch or break existing routing, 3D viewer, or leaflet integration.\n- Strictly remove the simulation card from Operator Dashboard.\n- Profile changes must persist across page refresh.\n- No user-style dragging on operator map.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 181
    included_step_index_end: 334
    user_requests: "Update the existing DropAid application. Fix the following issues without rebuilding the app or breaking working features.\n\n**1. Separate User and Operator Controls**\n- Remove all operator-only tools from the User Panel, including time skip, trip-stage simulation buttons, manual status controls, and reset controls.\n- Keep these tools exclusively in the Operator Panel or Demo Controls.\n- Ensure users can only access customer-facing booking and tracking features.\n\n**2. Lock Locations After Booking**\n- Before booking confirmation, allow users to edit pickup and destination locations.\n- Once a booking is submitted, lock both locations and prevent changes from the User Panel.\n- Display the confirmed pickup and destination as read-only.\n- Allow location changes only through an authorized operator workflow, with route recalculation and synchronized updates.\n\n**3. Restrict Cancellation After Pickup**\n- Allow users to cancel an eligible booking before the driver confirms patient pickup.\n- Once the patient is picked up, disable user cancellation and hide or remove the cancellation action.\n- Display a clear message: \"Your trip is in progress. Contact the assigned operator if assistance is required.\"\n- Enforce these rules in the booking logic, not just by hiding the button.\n\n**4. Remove Navbar Logo**\n- Remove the DropAid logo/icon from the navigation bar while preserving the DropAid text branding, alignment, and responsive layout.\n\n**Quality Control:** Test user and operator permissions, location locking, cancellation before and after pickup, route synchronization, and mobile responsiveness. Prevent unauthorized state changes, stale data, and duplicate actions. Fix all console errors and verify existing booking and tracking workflows still function correctly."
    user_requests: "Upgrade the existing DropAid application without rebuilding it or breaking current features.\n\n**1. Separate Operator and User Interfaces**\n- Give operators a dedicated dashboard with a fleet map, incoming requests, active trips, driver availability, and trip history.\n- Remove user-style location-dragging controls from the operator interface unless specifically needed for fleet management.\n- Automatically dispatch available ambulances to eligible requests using proximity and availability. Operators should monitor and override assignments when necessary, not manually approve every booking.\n- Keep user and operator permissions separate.\n\n**2. Automated Daily Ride Simulation**\n- Build a background simulation that generates approximately 20 realistic rides per simulated day, distributed randomly across different hours and minutes.\n- Simulate requests, ambulance assignment, pickup, hospital transit, and completion with realistic delays.\n- Randomize pickup locations, destinations, hospitals, and available ambulances.\n- Store every generated ride with a unique ID, timestamps, status history, assigned driver, ambulance, and hospital in persistent storage.\n- Display incoming, active, completed, and historical rides in the Operator Dashboard.\n- Provide Start, Pause, and Reset simulation controls in the operator/demo environment. Prevent duplicate rides and ensure timers do not multiply after navigation or refresh.\n- Clearly label generated records as simulated data. Do not claim the simulation runs continuously when the application or backend is inactive.\n\n**3. Hospital Directory**\n- Remove the entire \342\200\234Verified Hospital Directory (Delhi \302\267 Noida \302\267 Haryana)\342\200\235 section below the red booking button.\n- Make hospital listings accessible exclusively through the existing Hospitals navbar category.\n\n**4. Cloudinary Integration**\n- Verify end-to-end Cloudinary uploads, image previews, optimized delivery, and replacement for hospital, driver, and ambulance images.\n- Use secure backend-signed uploads or a restricted unsigned upload preset. Keep API secrets server-side.\n- Store returned Cloudinary asset URLs and public IDs in persistent database records.\n- Handle failed uploads, invalid files, missing configuration, and deletion/replacement safely.\n- Test actual uploads and retrieval; do not simulate successful uploads.\n\n**Quality Control:** Test automatic dispatch, operator overrides, ride persistence after refresh, simulation timing, duplicate prevention, hospital navigation, and Cloudinary upload/retrieval. Fix console errors and broken controls. Preserve responsive styling and clearly separate real bookings from simulated rides."
    user_requests: "Upgrade the existing DropAid application. Inspect the current code first, then implement these changes without rebuilding the application or breaking existing functionality.\n\n### 1. User Profile Management\nAllow users to view, edit, and save their personal profile, including name, phone number, email, profile photo, and emergency contact. Add a dedicated **My Profile** page accessible from the user navigation menu. Persist changes in the database and load saved information after refresh. Integrate Cloudinary for profile photo uploads with proper validation and secure configuration.\n\n### 2. Remove Simulation Card\nCompletely remove the **Automated Daily Ride Simulation** card from the Operator Dashboard, including its schedule, progress counters, speed controls, Pause, and Reset buttons. Preserve the fleet map, incoming requests, active trips, driver availability, trip history, and necessary administrative tools.\n\n### 3. Fix Actual Ambulance Movement\nThe route is visible, but the ambulance does not move correctly. Fix the underlying tracking logic:\n- Animate the vehicle marker continuously along the actual road-route coordinates returned by the routing service.\n- Progress from the starting point to the destination at a realistic, configurable speed.\n- Update the marker position, heading, remaining distance, ETA, and trip status.\n- Keep movement synchronized across User and Operator dashboards.\n- Prevent stale routes, frozen markers, duplicate timers, and movement restarting after component re-renders.\n- After pickup, recalculate the route from the ambulance\'s current position to the hospital.\n- Stop movement when the trip completes or is cancelled.\n\n### 4. Automatic Dispatch\nRemove the requirement for operators to manually start a simulation. Keep the application ready to receive bookings automatically.\n\nWhen a user submits a valid booking, automatically match the nearest available ambulance and assign its driver within **5 seconds**. Update the booking status and both dashboards immediately. If no ambulance is available or assignment fails, display a clear status and retry option rather than falsely confirming an assignment.\n\n### Quality Control\nTest profile editing and persistence, Cloudinary uploads, automatic assignment within five seconds, continuous road-following movement, pickup-to-hospital route transitions, dashboard synchronization, and trip completion. Fix console errors and duplicate timers. Clearly distinguish simulated vehicle movement from real GPS tracking. Preserve the existing responsive UI."
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
  }
}
