  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Core Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the core requirements, meticulously designing solutions. Specifically, I\'m focusing on user profile management, detailing functionalities like viewing, editing, and saving personal information, including name, phone number, email, and a profile photo. The photo aspect will integrate with Cloudinary, including image format validation and a preview function.\n\n\n**Refining Profile Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed personal health data into the \'My Profile\' page. This includes emergency contact information, blood type, allergies, medical conditions, and insurance details. The backend logic, particularly `server.ts` and API endpoints `/api/profile`, will handle GET and POST requests for profile persistence and retrieval. I\'m also ensuring saved information loads after a refresh using `localStorage`. I\'ve updated the `PatientProfile` interface in `src/types/index.ts` to reflect these added fields.\n\n\n**Implementing Profile Navigation**\n\nI\'ve updated the `src/types/index.ts` file to include \'profile\' as a view mode, and I\'ve added a \"My Profile\" button to the `Header.tsx` component for navigation. I\'ve also established GET and POST endpoints in `server.ts` to manage profile data, including an initial profile object. This includes all the fields needed, and also a profilePhoto.\n\n**Removing Simulation Card**\n\nI\'m removing the \"Automated Daily Ride Simulation\" card from `OperatorDashboard.tsx`. This includes the schedule, counters, and controls, ensuring that it doesn\'t appear anymore. I\'m focusing on preserving the essential features like the fleet map and administrative tools.\n\n\n**Refactoring Dashboard Display**\n\nI\'m currently streamlining the Operator Dashboard. I\'m removing the simulation header banner, replacing it with a cleaner command bar focused on real-time operational metrics. I\'m removing all simulation-related components and props in `OperatorDashboard.tsx`, streamlining the interface, and making sure the existing tabs are intact, maintaining functionality across \'fleet_map\', \'active_trips\', \'incoming\', \'fleet_units\', and \'history\' tabs. I\'ve removed the unused simulation props, and am verifying everything still renders as expected.\n\n\n**Animating Vehicle Movement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing continuous vehicle animation along the route. The goal is realistic movement at a configurable speed, updating position, heading, ETA, and status, and ensuring synchronization across both user and operator dashboards. I\'m actively addressing issues like stale routes and duplicate timers to ensure smooth animation and prevent restarts on re-renders. I\'m focusing on the actual animation logic in `App.tsx` and the relevant server-side operations, correcting the persistent interval to make the ambulance move as expected. After pick-up I\'ll make the new route to the destination.\n\n\n**Developing Movement Logic**\n\nI\'m now building the core logic for smooth ambulance movement. I\'m focusing on two states: `\'en_route_pickup\'` and `\'transporting\'`, where the ambulance follows the `booking.routePolyline`. The current vehicle position will advance along the polyline. I\'m implementing bearing calculation for heading updates, and updating location, heading, and speed, with ETA computation. I\'m making sure it can move forward correctly.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Phase Transitions**\n\nI\'m now implementing automatic state transitions. I\'m focusing on phase changes when the ambulance reaches the pickup and hospital locations. I\'m incorporating the transition logic from `\'en_route_pickup\'` to `\'on_scene\'` when within 35 meters, setting the speed to zero, and notifying the user. Transitioning to `\'transporting\'` will trigger a new route fetch to the hospital.\n\n\n**Finalizing Trip Completion**\n\nI\'m now completing the trip lifecycle by implementing final steps after handoff. I\'m focusing on setting the ambulance state to \'completed\' and then returning it to base bay availability. I\'m ensuring smooth synchronization between the User Dashboard and Operator Dashboard using LeafletMap, rendering ambulance markers based on location and heading, updating them in real-time. I\'m optimizing this through `marker.setLatLng`, and handling stale routes and duplicate timers by using a single `useRef` for the movement timer, clearing previous timers on unmount, and stopping movement upon trip completion or cancellation.\n\n\n**Automating Ambulance Matching**\n\nI\'m now integrating automated ambulance assignment. The system will match the closest available unit to a request within 5 seconds, updating booking status and both dashboards instantly. I\'m handling the scenarios of no ambulances available by displaying a clear status with a retry option. I\'m also implementing a radar dispatch animation for a \'pending\' booking state.\n\n\n"
