  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Map Functionality**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `LeafletMap.tsx` component and noticed the marker updates in response to `ambulances` changes, which is great! I\'m particularly interested in `ambulanceIcon` and its rotation and siren aura styling, specifically the `transform` and `transition` properties. I\'m also noting the `marker.setLatLng` function for positioning.\n\n\n**Investigating Animation Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into the continuous ambulance movement engine, specifically within `App.tsx`. I\'m focused on how active trips (user bookings or those en route) are handled using `routePolyline` and `currentWaypointIndex`. The 900ms tick and the calculation of how many points to step for realistic road movement are the current focus.\n\n\n**Refining Path Calculations**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the polyline path logic. I\'ve realized that moving one or two points per second provides smooth navigation along complex routes if the polyline contains many points, such as those found in Delhi\'s road network. I\'ve been refining the index increment using `Math.min` to stay within the polyline boundaries and have the current and previous points tracked. I am deep in the heading calculation and updating ambulance location, speed, and booking status. Next up, ETA calculations based on the remaining distance and estimated speed.\n\n\n**Evaluating Stage Transitions**\n\nI\'m now examining the state changes for an ambulance during a booking. I\'m focusing on the logic for progressing from \'en\\_route\\_pickup\' to \'on\\_scene\', handling pickup arrival, and updating the stage. I\'m noting the speed changes upon arrival, and the triggered toast notifications. The automatic transition to \'transporting\' after a short delay is the main focus, and the subsequent retrieval of the new hospital route and reset of the waypoint index.\n\n\n**Finalizing Ambulance Handover**\n\nI\'m now implementing the ambulance handoff at the hospital. I\'ve defined the logic for the \"transporting\" stage transition. Upon arrival, I update the stage, set speed to zero, and display a \"Trauma handoff in progress\" toast. A four-second delay then moves the stage to \"completed,\" and the ambulance is returned to \"available\" at its base. A \"Unit returned to service\" toast is triggered. I\'ve also added logic to immediately halt movement and release the ambulance to \"available\" if the booking is cancelled. Finally, I\'ve checked what happens during a 5 second booking hold. If no ambulances are available, the booking is created as pending.\n\n\n**Implementing Auto-Dispatch**\n\nI\'m now integrating an auto-dispatch feature for bookings when no ambulances are immediately available. My priority is handling the 5-second auto-matching, which includes creating a pending booking. I\'m focusing on the matching algorithm, booking updates with route details, and ambulance status changes (to \"en\\_route\\_pickup\"). I\'m also addressing the state updates to show \"matching\" progress, and the immediate start of the movement engine upon dispatch. Toast notifications are also being configured.\n\n\n**Integrating User Profile**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user profile functionality within `App.tsx`. I\'m focusing on the rendering of the `<UserProfileView>` based on the `currentView` state, and the handling of profile updates using the `POST /api/profile` endpoint, local storage, and state management. The `handleSaveProfile` function and the fetching and caching profile in the `useEffect` hook are the current focus. I\'m also confirming the `calculateBearing` helper function.\n\n\n"
