  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Booking Logic**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `handleCreateBooking` function within `src/App.tsx`. Initially, it was a bit rushed, instantly assigning ambulances. Now, I\'m working on a more robust approach. I\'m focusing on implementing a 5-second window for automatic matching, and handling the critical edge case of no available ambulances gracefully, complete with clear status updates and a retry option.\n\n\n**Implementing Ambulance Workflow**\n\nI\'ve finalized the \'no units available\' scenario, creating bookings with a \'pending\' stage, and a clear user message with a retry option. Now, I\'m focusing on the automatic matching workflow. I\'m aiming for a 3-4 second matching period, well within the 5-second countdown. If units are available, I\'ll create a \'pending\' booking, initiate the countdown, find the nearest unit, calculate the route, assign the unit, set the en route status, reset the countdown and begin vehicle movement, showing a toast to the user.\n\n\n"
